window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3"]={"id":"CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3","title":"CGL 13 OCT 2026 SHIFT 3","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000070981","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"Which of the following options matches the given address exactly?<br>Mr R. Das<br>55 Golden Garden, 2nd Floor<br>Malad West, Mumbai - 400064 [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा विकल्प दिए गए पते से ठीक मेल खाता है?<br>Mr R. Das<br>55 Golden Garden, 2nd Floor<br>Malad West, Mumbai - 400064 [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mr R. Das, 55 Golden Garden, 2nd Floor, Malad West, Mumbai - 400064"},"2":{"en":"Mr R. Das, 55 Golden Gardens, 2nd Floor, Malad West, Mumbai - 40064"},"3":{"en":"Mr R. Das, 55 Golden Garden, 2nd Floor, Malad West, Mumbai - 400065"},"4":{"en":"Mr R. Das, 55 Golden Garden, 3rd Floor, Malad West, Mumbai - 400064"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Option 1 copies the given address word for word<br>Option 2 writes 'Gardens' and PIN 40064, option 3 changes the PIN to 400065 and option 4 changes the floor to 3rd<br>So option 1 matches the address exactly<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Mr R. Das, 55 Golden Garden, 2nd Floor, Malad West, Mumbai - 400064.</b>","hi":"विकल्प 1 दिया गया पता शब्दशः दोहराता है<br>विकल्प 2 में 'Gardens' तथा पिन 40064, विकल्प 3 में पिन 400065 और विकल्प 4 में मंज़िल 3rd कर दी गई है<br>अतः विकल्प 1 पते से ठीक मेल खाता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): Mr R. Das, 55 Golden Garden, 2nd Floor, Malad West, Mumbai - 400064 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000070982","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"BRAVE\" is written as \"GWFAJ\". How will \"CLOUD\" be written in the same code language? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"किसी निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"BRAVE\" को \"GWFAJ\" लिखा जाता है। उसी कूट भाषा में \"CLOUD\" को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"HOTZJ"},"2":{"en":"HQSZJ"},"3":{"en":"HQTZI"},"4":{"en":"HOTZI"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Every letter moves five places forward: B→G, R→W, A→F, V→A, E→J<br>CLOUD gives C→H, L→Q, O→T, U→Z, D→I<br>Code = HQTZI<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): HQTZI.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक अक्षर पाँच स्थान आगे बढ़ता है: B→G, R→W, A→F, V→A, E→J<br>CLOUD से C→H, L→Q, O→T, U→Z, D→I<br>कूट = HQTZI<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): HQTZI है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000070983","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"INTELLIGENCE\" is written as \"JNUEMLJGFNDE\". How will \"EXPERIENCES\" be written? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"किसी निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"INTELLIGENCE\" को \"JNUEMLJGFNDE\" लिखा जाता है। \"EXPERIENCES\" को कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"FXQFSJFNDET"},"2":{"en":"FXPESIFNEET"},"3":{"en":"FXQESIFNDET"},"4":{"en":"FXQESJFENDFT"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Letters at odd places move one step forward and letters at even places stay unchanged: I→J, N→N, T→U, E→E, L→M, L→L, I→J, G→G, E→F, N→N, C→D, E→E<br>Applying the same rule to EXPERIENCES gives F X Q E S I F N D E T<br>Code = FXQESIFNDET<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): FXQESIFNDET.</b>","hi":"विषम स्थान के अक्षर एक कदम आगे बढ़ते हैं और सम स्थान के अक्षर वैसे ही रहते हैं: I→J, N→N, T→U, E→E, L→M, L→L, I→J, G→G, E→F, N→N, C→D, E→E<br>यही नियम EXPERIENCES पर लगाने से F X Q E S I F N D E T मिलता है<br>कूट = FXQESIFNDET<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): FXQESIFNDET है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000070984","section":"REASONING","topic":"Order & Ranking","question":{"en":"There are 60 students in a class. If Neha is 25th from the top, find her rank from the bottom. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक कक्षा में 60 विद्यार्थी हैं। यदि नेहा ऊपर से 25वें स्थान पर है, तो नीचे से उसका स्थान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"34th","hi":"34वाँ"},"2":{"en":"35th","hi":"35वाँ"},"3":{"en":"36th","hi":"36वाँ"},"4":{"en":"37th","hi":"37वाँ"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Rank from bottom = total − rank from top + 1<br>= 60 − 25 + 1 = 36th<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 36th.</b>","hi":"नीचे से स्थान = कुल − ऊपर से स्थान + 1<br>= 60 − 25 + 1 = 36वाँ<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 36वाँ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000070985","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"How should an administrative officer respond effectively and empathetically when a large, frustrated crowd gathers at a public grievance window due to a digital server crash delaying certificate issuance? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"जब डिजिटल सर्वर ठप होने से प्रमाणपत्र जारी करने में देरी के कारण जन-शिकायत काउंटर पर बड़ी संख्या में नाराज़ लोग एकत्र हो जाएँ, तो एक प्रशासनिक अधिकारी को प्रभावी और सहानुभूतिपूर्ण ढंग से क्या प्रतिक्रिया देनी चाहिए? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Deploy security personnel immediately to clear the area and protect the office property from potential damage.","hi":"संभावित क्षति से कार्यालय की संपत्ति बचाने के लिए तुरंत सुरक्षा कर्मी तैनात कर क्षेत्र खाली कराएँ।"},"2":{"en":"Announce the technical issue clearly, acknowledge their frustration, and provide a realistic manual alternative or timeline.","hi":"तकनीकी समस्या स्पष्ट रूप से बताएँ, उनकी नाराज़गी स्वीकार करें और व्यावहारिक मैन्युअल विकल्प या समय-सीमा दें।"},"3":{"en":"Retreat to the inner office until the technical team resolves the server crash to avoid personal confrontation.","hi":"आमना-सामना टालने के लिए तब तक भीतरी कार्यालय में चले जाएँ जब तक तकनीकी टीम सर्वर ठीक न कर दे।"},"4":{"en":"Promise immediate delivery of all certificates within an hour to temporarily calm down the agitated gathering.","hi":"नाराज़ भीड़ को शांत करने के लिए एक घंटे में सभी प्रमाणपत्र देने का तुरंत वादा करें।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The crowd is angry because the work is stuck, so the officer must first inform them honestly about the technical problem<br>Acknowledging their frustration and offering a realistic manual option or a clear timeline respects both their time and the rules<br>Force, escape or a false promise only increases the trouble, so this is the most effective and empathetic response<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Announce the technical issue clearly, acknowledge their frustration, and provide a realistic manual alternative or timeline.</b>","hi":"भीड़ इसलिए नाराज़ है कि काम रुका हुआ है, अतः अधिकारी को पहले तकनीकी समस्या के बारे में ईमानदारी से बताना चाहिए<br>नाराज़गी स्वीकार करके व्यावहारिक मैन्युअल विकल्प या स्पष्ट समय-सीमा देना उनके समय और नियम दोनों का सम्मान है<br>बल प्रयोग, भाग जाना या झूठा वादा केवल परेशानी बढ़ाते हैं, अतः यही सबसे प्रभावी और सहानुभूतिपूर्ण प्रतिक्रिया है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): तकनीकी समस्या स्पष्ट रूप से बताएँ, उनकी नाराज़गी स्वीकार करें और व्यावहारिक मैन्युअल विकल्प या समय-सीमा दें। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000070986","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Your team's three-month effort on a major development proposal is completely rejected by the ministry without explanation. As an emotionally intelligent leader, how can you best maintain team morale and long-term engagement? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक बड़े विकास प्रस्ताव पर आपकी टीम के तीन महीने के परिश्रम को मंत्रालय ने बिना किसी स्पष्टीकरण के पूरी तरह अस्वीकार कर दिया। एक भावनात्मक रूप से बुद्धिमान नेता के रूप में आप टीम का मनोबल और दीर्घकालिक जुड़ाव कैसे बनाए रखेंगे? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Express frustration regarding the ministry's lack of transparency to mirror the team's disappointment, aiming to build a sense of unity by collectively positioning yourselves as the \"victims\" of an unfair process.","hi":"मंत्रालय की अपारदर्शिता पर नाराज़गी व्यक्त करके टीम की निराशा का साथ दें, जिससे सब मिलकर स्वयं को अन्यायपूर्ण प्रक्रिया के \"शिकार\" के रूप में देख सकें।"},"2":{"en":"Facilitate an open reflection session to acknowledge the emotional weight of the rejection, validate the team's hard work, and pivot the focus toward synthesising the lessons learned and refining the strategy for future opportunities.","hi":"एक खुला चिंतन सत्र कराएँ जिसमें अस्वीकृति के भावनात्मक बोझ को स्वीकारा जाए, टीम के परिश्रम को सराहा जाए और ध्यान भविष्य के अवसरों के लिए सीख तथा रणनीति सुधारने पर केंद्रित किया जाए।"},"3":{"en":"Pivot immediately to a new, unrelated project to avoid dwelling on the past, intentionally suppressing discussions about the rejection to maintain a culture of relentless forward momentum and avoid potential loss of confidence.","hi":"बीते हुए कल पर विचार न करने के लिए तुरंत किसी नए, असंबंधित प्रोजेक्ट पर लग जाएँ और अस्वीकृति की चर्चा दबा दें ताकि आगे बढ़ने की गति बनी रहे।"},"4":{"en":"Conduct a forensic post-mortem to identify individual shortcomings or errors that may have led to the rejection, ensuring that team members understand where their personal contributions fell short of the mark.","hi":"अस्वीकृति के कारणों को खोजने के लिए विस्तृत पोस्ट-मॉर्टम करें और बताएँ कि किस व्यक्ति के योगदान में कहाँ कमी रह गई।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The team needs its effort to be recognised before any new plan is made, so an open reflection that validates the hard work keeps trust intact<br>Converting the setback into lessons and a better strategy for the next opportunity keeps long-term engagement alive<br>Blaming the ministry, suppressing the feeling or hunting for individual faults all damage morale<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Facilitate an open reflection session to acknowledge the emotional weight of the rejection, validate the team's hard work, and pivot the focus toward synthesising the lessons learned and refining the strategy for future opportunities.</b>","hi":"नई योजना बनाने से पहले टीम को अपने परिश्रम की स्वीकृति चाहिए, अतः परिश्रम को सराहने वाला खुला चिंतन विश्वास बनाए रखता है<br>असफलता को सीख और अगले अवसर के लिए बेहतर रणनीति में बदलने से दीर्घकालिक जुड़ाव बना रहता है<br>मंत्रालय को दोष देना, भावनाएँ दबाना या व्यक्तिगत गलतियाँ खोजना मनोबल को नुकसान पहुँचाता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): एक खुला चिंतन सत्र कराएँ जिसमें अस्वीकृति के भावनात्मक बोझ को स्वीकारा जाए, टीम के परिश्रम को सराहा जाए और ध्यान भविष्य के अवसरों के लिए सीख तथा रणनीति सुधारने पर केंद्रित किया जाए। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000070987","section":"REASONING","topic":"Counting Figures","question":{"en":"How many triangles are there in the given figure?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दी गई आकृति में कितने त्रिभुज हैं?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In the main triangle one horizontal line and one vertical midline divide the upper part into 6 small triangles<br>Joining these 6 small triangles two at a time gives 6 more triangles, and taking the whole main triangle gives 3 triangles of different sizes, so 15 triangles come from the main triangle<br>The band at the base below the horizontal lines gives 3 more triangles and each of the two curved wings gives 3 triangles<br>Total = 15 + 3 + 6 = 24<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7_opt4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"मुख्य त्रिभुज में एक क्षैतिज रेखा और एक ऊर्ध्वाधर मध्य-रेखा ऊपरी भाग को 6 छोटे त्रिभुजों में बाँटती हैं<br>इन 6 छोटे त्रिभुजों को दो-दो मिलाने से 6 और त्रिभुज तथा पूरा मुख्य त्रिभुज लेने पर 3 त्रिभुज मिलते हैं, अतः मुख्य त्रिभुज से 15 त्रिभुज बनते हैं<br>क्षैतिज रेखाओं के नीचे का आधार पट्टा 3 और त्रिभुज देता है तथा दोनों घुमावदार पंखों से 3-3 त्रिभुज मिलते हैं<br>कुल = 15 + 3 + 6 = 24<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7_opt4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q7_opt4.jpg"]}},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000070988","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"During a professional team discussion, a female colleague is frequently interrupted and talked over by male team members. Although she visibly attempts to re-enter the conversation multiple times, she fails to gain the floor. What is the most appropriate action for you to take? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक पेशेवर टीम चर्चा के दौरान एक महिला सहकर्मी को पुरुष सदस्य बार-बार टोकते हैं और उनकी बात काटते हैं। वह स्पष्ट रूप से कई बार बोलने का प्रयास करती है, परंतु बोल नहीं पाती। आपके लिए सबसे उपयुक्त कार्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Choose to let the incident pass without any intervention, justifying your inaction by assuming that this is simply the natural way professional discussions function sometimes.","hi":"इस घटना को बिना किसी हस्तक्षेप के जाने दें, यह मानकर अपनी निष्क्रियता को उचित ठहराएँ कि पेशेवर चर्चाओं में कभी-कभी ऐसा होता ही है।"},"2":{"en":"Directly confront the male team members in front of everyone and aggressively tell them to stop interrupting the female colleague while she is trying to speak.","hi":"सबके सामने पुरुष सदस्यों से सीधे आक्रामक रूप से कहें कि सहकर्मी के बोलते समय टोकना बंद करें।"},"3":{"en":"Suggest to the female colleague privately that she should attempt to speak much more assertively in future meetings to ensure her voice is heard by others.","hi":"महिला सहकर्मी को निजी में सुझाव दें कि आगे की बैठकों में वे अधिक दृढ़ता से बोलें ताकि उनकी बात सुनी जाए।"},"4":{"en":"Publicly acknowledge the value of her contribution and actively invite her to complete her thoughts, thereby ensuring she has the opportunity to speak to the group.","hi":"सार्वजनिक रूप से उनके योगदान का मूल्य स्वीकार करें और सक्रिय रूप से उन्हें अपनी बात पूरी करने के लिए आमंत्रित करें, जिससे उन्हें समूह के समक्ष बोलने का अवसर मिले।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"A leader's duty is to protect equal participation, so quietly ignoring the interruption allows the unfair practice to continue<br>Acknowledgement followed by a clear invitation gives the colleague the floor without humiliating anyone, so the discussion stays respectful<br>The other options either normalise the behaviour, escalate it aggressively or shift the blame to the colleague<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Publicly acknowledge the value of her contribution and actively invite her to complete her thoughts, thereby ensuring she has the opportunity to speak to the group.</b>","hi":"नेता का दायित्व समान भागीदारी की रक्षा करना है, अतः चुपचाप अनदेखा करना अनुचित व्यवहार को जारी रखने देता है<br>स्वीकृति के साथ स्पष्ट आमंत्रण सहकर्मी को बोलने का अवसर देता है और किसी का अपमान भी नहीं होता<br>अन्य विकल्प या तो व्यवहार को सामान्य बनाते हैं, या आक्रामक रूप से बढ़ा देते हैं, या दोष सहकर्मी पर डाल देते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): सार्वजनिक रूप से उनके योगदान का मूल्य स्वीकार करें और सक्रिय रूप से उन्हें अपनी बात पूरी करने के लिए आमंत्रित करें, जिससे उन्हें समूह के समक्ष बोलने का अवसर मिले। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000070989","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Completing","question":{"en":"Complete the pattern in fig. (X) by selecting one of the figures from the four alternatives :<br>Figure(X):<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q9.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आकृति (X) का पैटर्न चार विकल्पों में से एक आकृति चुनकर पूरा कीजिए :<br>आकृति (X):<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q9.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In the lower part of figure (X) two dots lie at the two lower corners and three lines rise from the base to meet at a single upper point<br>The missing upper part must therefore be a small pentagon carrying one dot on the left and one dot on the right, with the meeting point of the lines just below it<br>Only option 1 keeps both dots at the same height and the converging lines at the same place, so it completes the pattern<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q9_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"आकृति (X) के निचले भाग में दो बिंदु दोनों निचले कोनों पर हैं और तीन रेखाएँ आधार से उठकर एक ही ऊपरी बिंदु पर मिलती हैं<br>अतः लुप्त ऊपरी भाग छोटा पंचभुज होना चाहिए जिसके बाएँ एक और दाएँ एक बिंदु हो तथा रेखाओं का मिलन-बिंदु उसके ठीक नीचे हो<br>केवल विकल्प 1 में दोनों बिंदु समान ऊँचाई पर और मिलती रेखाएँ उसी स्थान पर हैं, अतः यही पैटर्न पूरा करता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q9_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q9.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q9_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q9_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q9_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q9_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q9_opt1.jpg"]}},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000070990","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If the symbols are defined such that α represents addition, β represents subtraction, γ represents multiplication, and δ represents division, then compute the value of the expression.<br>100 δ 5 γ 4 α 20 β 10 [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि प्रतीकों को इस प्रकार परिभाषित किया गया है कि α जोड़, β घटाना, γ गुणा और δ भाग को दर्शाता है, तो व्यंजक का मान ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>100 δ 5 γ 4 α 20 β 10 [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"80"},"2":{"en":"90"},"3":{"en":"100"},"4":{"en":"110"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Replacing the symbols: \\(100 \\div 5 \\times 4 + 20 - 10\\)<br>\\(100 \\div 5 = 20\\) and \\(20 \\times 4 = 80\\)<br>\\(80 + 20 - 10 = 90\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 90.</b>","hi":"प्रतीकों को बदलने पर: \\(100 \\div 5 \\times 4 + 20 - 10\\)<br>\\(100 \\div 5 = 20\\) तथा \\(20 \\times 4 = 80\\)<br>\\(80 + 20 - 10 = 90\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 90 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000070991","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If 32 + 41 = 20; 25 + 34 = 28; 62 + 15 = 28, then find the value of 53 + 46. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि 32 + 41 = 20; 25 + 34 = 28; 62 + 15 = 28 है, तो 53 + 46 का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"36"},"2":{"en":"42"},"3":{"en":"48"},"4":{"en":"32"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"All the digits of the two numbers are added and the sum is doubled<br>32 + 41 : 3 + 2 + 4 + 1 = 10, 10 × 2 = 20 ✔; 25 + 34 : 14 × 2 = 28 ✔; 62 + 15 : 14 × 2 = 28 ✔<br>53 + 46 : 5 + 3 + 4 + 6 = 18, 18 × 2 = 36<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 36.</b>","hi":"दोनों संख्याओं के सभी अंक जोड़कर योग को दोगुना किया जाता है<br>32 + 41 : 3 + 2 + 4 + 1 = 10, 10 × 2 = 20 ✔; 25 + 34 : 14 × 2 = 28 ✔; 62 + 15 : 14 × 2 = 28 ✔<br>53 + 46 : 5 + 3 + 4 + 6 = 18, 18 × 2 = 36<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 36 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000070992","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"In the following question, one statement is given, followed by certain inferences. Consider the statement to be true even if it seems to contradict commonly known facts. Read the inferences carefully and decide which of them logically follow from the given statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>In recent quarters, sales of electric scooters have increased significantly in both urban and semi-urban regions due to rising fuel prices and improved battery technology offered by manufacturers.<br><b>Inferences:</b><br>I. The rise in electric scooter sales has reduced the sales of petrol scooters of all other companies.<br>II. Electric scooters were not available in the market earlier. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में एक कथन और उसके बाद कुछ अनुमान दिए गए हैं। कथन को सत्य मानिए, भले ही वह सामान्यतः ज्ञात तथ्यों के विपरीत प्रतीत हो। अनुमानों को ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि उनमें से कौन-से तार्किक रूप से कथन से निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>हाल की तिमाहियों में बढ़ती ईंधन कीमतों तथा निर्माताओं द्वारा दी गई बेहतर बैटरी तकनीक के कारण शहरी और अर्ध-शहरी दोनों क्षेत्रों में इलेक्ट्रिक स्कूटरों की बिक्री में उल्लेखनीय वृद्धि हुई है।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. इलेक्ट्रिक स्कूटरों की बिक्री बढ़ने से अन्य सभी कंपनियों के पेट्रोल स्कूटरों की बिक्री घटी है।<br>II. इलेक्ट्रिक स्कूटर पहले बाज़ार में उपलब्ध नहीं थे। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Inference I follows.","hi":"केवल अनुमान I निकलता है।"},"2":{"en":"Only Inference II follows.","hi":"केवल अनुमान II निकलता है।"},"3":{"en":"Both Inferences I and II follow.","hi":"अनुमान I और II दोनों निकलते हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Neither Inference I nor Inference II follows.","hi":"न तो अनुमान I और न ही अनुमान II निकलता है।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The statement speaks only about electric scooter sales rising, and says nothing about the sales of petrol scooters of other companies, so I does not follow<br>The rise is credited to improved battery technology, which means such scooters were already being sold earlier, so II does not follow<br>Hence neither inference follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Neither Inference I nor Inference II follows.</b>","hi":"कथन केवल इलेक्ट्रिक स्कूटरों की बिक्री बढ़ने की बात करता है और अन्य कंपनियों के पेट्रोल स्कूटरों की बिक्री के बारे में कुछ नहीं कहता, अतः I नहीं निकलता<br>वृद्धि का कारण बेहतर बैटरी तकनीक बताया गया है, जिसका अर्थ है कि ऐसे स्कूटर पहले भी बिक रहे थे, अतः II नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए कोई भी अनुमान नहीं निकलता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): न तो अनुमान I और न ही अनुमान II निकलता है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000070993","section":"REASONING","topic":"Paper Folding, Cutting & Mirror/Water Images","question":{"en":"If a mirror is placed on the line XY, which figure will be the mirror image of the question figure?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q13.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि रेखा XY पर दर्पण रखा जाए, तो कौन-सी आकृति प्रश्न आकृति का दर्पण प्रतिबिम्ब होगी?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q13.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The mirror is vertical, so the order of the characters is reversed and each character is flipped left to right<br>The image must therefore begin with the mirror of 5 and end with the mirror of Z<br>Only option 2 reverses the whole group and flips every character, so it is the correct mirror image<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q13_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"दर्पण ऊर्ध्वाधर है, अतः अक्षरों/अंकों का क्रम उलट जाता है और प्रत्येक प्रतिबिम्बित होता है<br>इसलिए प्रतिबिम्ब 5 के दर्पण से आरम्भ होकर Z के दर्पण पर समाप्त होना चाहिए<br>केवल विकल्प 2 में पूरा समूह उलटा है और प्रत्येक अक्षर/अंक प्रतिबिम्बित है, अतः यही सही दर्पण प्रतिबिम्ब है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q13_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q13.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q13_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q13_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q13_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q13_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q13_opt2.jpg"]}},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000070994","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"You are working on a high-priority project with a tight deadline. Your colleague, who is responsible for the final quality audit, asks you to skip a few minor verification steps so they can leave early for a personal engagement. What should you do? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आप कड़ी समय-सीमा वाले एक अत्यंत प्राथमिकता के प्रोजेक्ट पर काम कर रहे हैं। अंतिम गुणवत्ता ऑडिट के लिए उत्तरदायी आपका सहकर्मी आपसे कुछ छोटे सत्यापन चरण छोड़ने के लिए कहता है ताकि वह किसी व्यक्तिगत कार्य के लिए जल्दी जा सके। आपको क्या करना चाहिए? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Skip the steps to maintain the team's friendly relationship.","hi":"टीम के मैत्रीपूर्ण संबंध बनाए रखने के लिए चरण छोड़ दें।"},"2":{"en":"Politely decline and explain the risks of bypassing the audit.","hi":"विनम्रता से मना करें और ऑडिट छोड़ने के जोखिम समझाएँ।"},"3":{"en":"Inform the supervisor about your colleague's unprofessional request.","hi":"सहकर्मी के अव्यावसायिक अनुरोध की जानकारी पर्यवेक्षक को दें।"},"4":{"en":"Complete the skipped steps yourself without informing anyone.","hi":"बिना किसी को बताए छोड़े गए चरण स्वयं पूरे कर लें।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Quality verification cannot be skipped merely for personal convenience, so agreeing to skip it puts the whole project at risk<br>Refusing politely and explaining the risk protects the work as well as the working relationship<br>Complaining to the supervisor or secretly covering up the gap only creates new problems<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Politely decline and explain the risks of bypassing the audit.</b>","hi":"व्यक्तिगत सुविधा के लिए गुणवत्ता सत्यापन छोड़ा नहीं जा सकता, अतः छोड़ने पर पूरा प्रोजेक्ट जोखिम में पड़ जाता है<br>विनम्रता से मना करके जोखिम समझाना काम तथा कार्य-संबंध दोनों की रक्षा करता है<br>पर्यवेक्षक से शिकायत करना या चुपचाप कमी पूरी कर लेना नई समस्याएँ पैदा करता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): विनम्रता से मना करें और ऑडिट छोड़ने के जोखिम समझाएँ। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000070995","section":"REASONING","topic":"Embedded Figures","question":{"en":"Carefully observe Figure (X) and identify the option figure in which Figure (X) is embedded exactly as shown.<br>Figure X:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q15.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"आकृति (X) को ध्यान से देखिए और वह विकल्प आकृति पहचानिए जिसमें आकृति (X) ठीक उसी रूप में अंतर्निहित है।<br>आकृति X:<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q15.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Figure (X) is a square with a vertical line on its left side and a slanting line rising from the lower-left corner to the middle of the top side<br>The answer figure must contain this square along with both these lines in the same position<br>Only option 2 has a square whose diagonals supply exactly these two lines, so figure (X) is embedded there<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q15_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"आकृति (X) एक वर्ग है जिसकी बाईं भुजा पर एक खड़ी रेखा है और निचले-बाएँ कोने से ऊपरी भुजा के मध्य तक एक तिरछी रेखा है<br>उत्तर आकृति में यह वर्ग तथा दोनों रेखाएँ उसी स्थिति में होनी चाहिए<br>केवल विकल्प 2 के वर्ग के विकर्ण ठीक यही दो रेखाएँ देते हैं, अतः वहीं आकृति (X) अंतर्निहित है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q15_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q15.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q15_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q15_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q15_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q15_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q15_opt2.jpg"]}},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000070996","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In the following question, out of the five figures marked (a), (b), (c), (d), and (e), four are similar in a certain manner. However, one figure is not like the other four. Choose the figure which is different from the rest.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q16.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में (a), (b), (c), (d) और (e) से अंकित पाँच आकृतियों में से चार किसी प्रकार एक जैसी हैं। परंतु एक आकृति शेष चारों जैसी नहीं है। वह आकृति चुनिए जो शेष से भिन्न है।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q16.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In four of the figures the inner lines join one corner or vertex of the outer figure to the opposite corner, so the parts on the two sides of every line are equal<br>In option 1 the chords are drawn inside a circle in such a way that the parts cut off are unequal, so this figure has no such symmetry<br>Hence the figure in option 1 is different from the rest<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q16_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"चार आकृतियों में भीतरी रेखाएँ बाहरी आकृति के एक कोने या शीर्ष को उसके विपरीत कोने से जोड़ती हैं, अतः प्रत्येक रेखा के दोनों ओर के भाग बराबर हैं<br>विकल्प 1 में जीवाएँ वृत्त के भीतर इस प्रकार खींची गई हैं कि कटे हुए भाग असमान हैं, अतः इस आकृति में यह सममिति नहीं है<br>इसलिए विकल्प 1 की आकृति शेष से भिन्न है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q16_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q16.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q16_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q16_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q16_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q16_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q16_opt1.jpg"]}},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000070997","section":"REASONING","topic":"Venn Diagrams","question":{"en":"The following diagram shows the number of children playing Basketball, Cricket, Football, and Volleyball.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]<br>If the total number of children is 500, what is the percentage of children playing at least two games? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित आकृति में बास्केटबॉल, क्रिकेट, फुटबॉल और वॉलीबॉल खेलने वाले बच्चों की संख्या दर्शाई गई है।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]<br>यदि बच्चों की कुल संख्या 500 है, तो कम से कम दो खेल खेलने वाले बच्चों का प्रतिशत क्या है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The regions where two or three circles overlap carry 12, 15, 5, 8, 6 and 10 children<br>Children playing at least two games = 12 + 15 + 5 + 8 + 6 + 10 = 56<br>Percentage = \\(\\frac{56}{500} \\times 100 = 11.2\\%\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"जहाँ दो या तीन वृत्त एक-दूसरे को काटते हैं, वहाँ 12, 15, 5, 8, 6 तथा 10 बच्चे हैं<br>कम से कम दो खेल खेलने वाले बच्चे = 12 + 15 + 5 + 8 + 6 + 10 = 56<br>प्रतिशत = \\(\\frac{56}{500} \\times 100 = 11.2\\%\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg"]}},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000070998","section":"REASONING","topic":"Dice & Cube","question":{"en":"Four different positions of the same dice are shown. Select the number that will be on the face opposite to the one showing '4'.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q18.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक ही पासे की चार अलग-अलग स्थितियाँ दिखाई गई हैं। वह संख्या चुनिए जो '4' दर्शाने वाले फलक के विपरीत फलक पर होगी।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q18.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"From the four positions, the faces seen next to 4 are 5, 2 and 6<br>So 4 is adjacent to 5, 2 and 6, and the only number left is 1<br>Hence 1 lies on the face opposite to 4<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"चारों स्थितियों से 4 के साथ दिखने वाले फलक 5, 2 तथा 6 हैं<br>अतः 4, फलक 5, 2 और 6 के आसन्न है और शेष बचती है केवल 1<br>इसलिए 4 के विपरीत फलक पर 1 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q18.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt2.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q18_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt1.jpg"]}},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000070999","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"In the following question, out of the five figures marked (a), (b), (c), (d), and (e), four are similar in a certain manner. However, one figure is not like the other four. Choose the figure which is different from the rest.<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q19.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में (a), (b), (c), (d) और (e) से अंकित पाँच आकृतियों में से चार किसी प्रकार एक जैसी हैं। परंतु एक आकृति शेष चारों जैसी नहीं है। वह आकृति चुनिए जो शेष से भिन्न है।<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q19.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In four of the figures the two ends of the slanting line carry the same symbol — two dots, two squares, two stars and two triangular arrow heads<br>In option 1 one end carries a diamond and the other end carries a dot, so the two symbols are different<br>Hence the figure in option 1 is different from the rest<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q19_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"चार आकृतियों में तिरछी रेखा के दोनों सिरों पर एक ही प्रतीक है — दो बिंदु, दो वर्ग, दो तारे तथा दो त्रिभुजाकार तीर<br>विकल्प 1 में एक सिरे पर हीरा और दूसरे सिरे पर बिंदु है, अतः दोनों प्रतीक भिन्न हैं<br>इसलिए विकल्प 1 की आकृति शेष से भिन्न है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q16_opt4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q19.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q19_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q19_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q19_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q19_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q19_opt1.jpg","https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q16_opt4.jpg"]}},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000071000","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"Read the given statement carefully and the following assumptions based on it. Decide which of the assumptions are implicit in the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>Give adequate job related training to the employees before assigning them full fledged work.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. Training helps in boosting the performance of employees.<br>II. Employees have no skill sets before training is provided to them. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दिया गया कथन ध्यान से पढ़िए और उस पर आधारित अनुमानों को देखिए। निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-से अनुमान कथन में निहित हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>कर्मचारियों को पूर्ण कार्य सौंपने से पहले उन्हें पर्याप्त कार्य-संबंधी प्रशिक्षण दें।<br><b>अनुमान:</b><br>I. प्रशिक्षण कर्मचारियों के कार्य-निष्पादन को बढ़ाने में सहायक है।<br>II. प्रशिक्षण मिलने से पहले कर्मचारियों में कोई कौशल नहीं होता। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Assumption I is implicit","hi":"केवल अनुमान I निहित है"},"2":{"en":"Both Assumptions I and II are implicit","hi":"अनुमान I और II दोनों निहित हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only Assumption II is implicit","hi":"केवल अनुमान II निहित है"},"4":{"en":"Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit","hi":"न तो अनुमान I और न ही II निहित है"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Training is advised before full work is given because it improves the performance of the employees, so I is implicit<br>The statement never says that the employees are completely without skills, so II is only a stretch<br>Hence only assumption I is implicit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only Assumption I is implicit.</b>","hi":"पूर्ण कार्य देने से पहले प्रशिक्षण इसलिए सुझाया गया है क्योंकि यह कर्मचारियों का निष्पादन सुधारता है, अतः I निहित है<br>कथन कहीं नहीं कहता कि कर्मचारियों में कोई कौशल ही नहीं है, अतः II निहित नहीं है<br>इसलिए केवल अनुमान I निहित है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल अनुमान I निहित है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000071001","section":"REASONING","topic":"Matrix","question":{"en":"Which of the following rows/columns are connected/related with each other in some way?<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Rows</td><td colspan=\"5\" style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px;text-align:center\">Columns</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">14</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">14</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी पंक्तियाँ/स्तंभ किसी प्रकार एक-दूसरे से जुड़े/संबंधित हैं?<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td rowspan=\"2\" style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">Rows</td><td colspan=\"5\" style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px;text-align:center\">Columns</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">I</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">3</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">II</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">7</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">14</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">III</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">5</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">8</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">IV</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">15</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">18</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">13</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">V</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">9</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">11</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">14</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">10</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Columns I, II and III","hi":"स्तंभ I, II और III"},"2":{"en":"Columns I, III and IV","hi":"स्तंभ I, III और IV"},"3":{"en":"Columns II, IV and V","hi":"स्तंभ II, IV और V"},"4":{"en":"Columns II, III and IV","hi":"स्तंभ II, III और IV"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In every row, column III is column I plus 7 and column IV is column I plus 5<br>Row I: 3 + 7 = 10 and 3 + 5 = 8; row IV: 11 + 7 = 18 and 11 + 5 = 16, and the same holds in the remaining rows<br>So columns I, III and IV are related to each other<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Columns I, III and IV.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पंक्ति में स्तंभ III = स्तंभ I + 7 तथा स्तंभ IV = स्तंभ I + 5 है<br>पंक्ति I: 3 + 7 = 10 और 3 + 5 = 8; पंक्ति IV: 11 + 7 = 18 और 11 + 5 = 16, तथा शेष पंक्तियों में भी यही लागू है<br>अतः स्तंभ I, III और IV परस्पर संबंधित हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): स्तंभ I, III और IV है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000071002","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, there is a specific relationship between the first two figures. Establish a similar relationship between the third and fourth figures by selecting a suitable figure from the given Answer Figures to replace the question mark (?).<br><b>Question Figures:</b><br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q22.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में पहली दो आकृतियों के बीच एक विशिष्ट संबंध है। तीसरी और चौथी आकृति के बीच भी वही संबंध स्थापित कीजिए और प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर दी गई उत्तर आकृतियों में से उपयुक्त आकृति चुनिए।<br><b>प्रश्न आकृतियाँ:</b><br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q22.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In (A) the small dot lies at the top-left corner and a cross is drawn at the lower end of the slanting line; in (B) the dot has moved to the top-right corner and the cross has also shifted with the slanting line, i.e. both small elements are mirrored<br>Applying the same mirror movement to (C), where a diamond sits at the top-right and a small figure at the lower end of the slanting line, gives the diamond at the top-left and the dark dot with its slanting stroke at the bottom<br>Answer figure 2 shows exactly this arrangement<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"आकृति (A) में छोटा बिंदु ऊपर-बाएँ कोने पर है और तिरछी रेखा के निचले सिरे पर क्रॉस है; आकृति (B) में बिंदु ऊपर-दाएँ कोने पर चला गया है और क्रॉस भी तिरछी रेखा के साथ खिसक गया है, अर्थात दोनों छोटे अंश दर्पण रूप में बदल गए हैं<br>यही दर्पण गति आकृति (C) पर लगाने से, जिसमें हीरा ऊपर-दाएँ तथा तिरछी रेखा के निचले सिरे पर छोटी आकृति है, हीरा ऊपर-बाएँ तथा नीचे गहरा बिंदु अपनी तिरछी पट्टी के साथ आ जाता है<br>उत्तर आकृति 2 में ठीक यही व्यवस्था है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q22.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt2.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg"]}},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000071003","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, there is a specific relationship between the first two figures. Establish a similar relationship between the third and fourth figures by selecting a suitable figure from the given Answer Figures to replace the question mark (?).<br><b>Question Figures:</b><br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q23.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में पहली दो आकृतियों के बीच एक विशिष्ट संबंध है। तीसरी और चौथी आकृति के बीच भी वही संबंध स्थापित कीजिए और प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर दी गई उत्तर आकृतियों में से उपयुक्त आकृति चुनिए।<br><b>प्रश्न आकृतियाँ:</b><br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q23.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"In (A) the three shapes stand as triangle, square, circle and in (B) the third shape (circle) becomes the outer boundary, the second shape (square) goes at the top inside it and the first shape (triangle) goes at the bottom<br>In (C) the shapes are square, circle, triangle, so the triangle must become the outer boundary, the circle must sit at the top inside and the square at the bottom<br>Answer figure 3 shows exactly this arrangement<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"आकृति (A) में तीन आकृतियाँ त्रिभुज, वर्ग, वृत्त के क्रम में हैं और आकृति (B) में तीसरी आकृति (वृत्त) बाहरी सीमा बनती है, दूसरी आकृति (वर्ग) उसके भीतर ऊपर जाती है और पहली आकृति (त्रिभुज) नीचे<br>आकृति (C) में क्रम वर्ग, वृत्त, त्रिभुज है, अतः त्रिभुज बाहरी सीमा बनेगा, वृत्त भीतर ऊपर तथा वर्ग नीचे होगा<br>उत्तर आकृति 3 में ठीक यही व्यवस्था है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt2.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q23.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q21_opt1.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2/q18_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-12-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q17_opt2.jpg"]}},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000071004","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Fill in the blanks (_) using one of the following four options such that the series follows a specific pattern in the given order.<br>a_bcad_cadb_ _dbc [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दिए गए क्रम में श्रेणी एक विशिष्ट पैटर्न का पालन करे, इसके लिए निम्नलिखित चार विकल्पों में से एक से रिक्त स्थान (_) भरिए।<br>a_bcad_cadb_ _dbc [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"dbca"},"2":{"en":"adbc"},"3":{"en":"acdb"},"4":{"en":"dcba"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Putting d, b, c, a in the four blanks gives a d b c a d b c a d b c a d b c<br>The series is made of the repeating block 'adbc' written four times, so the pattern stays the same throughout<br>Hence d, b, c, a fills the blanks correctly<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): dbca.</b>","hi":"चार रिक्त स्थानों में d, b, c, a भरने पर a d b c a d b c a d b c a d b c प्राप्त होता है<br>श्रेणी चार बार दोहराए गए खंड 'adbc' से बनी है, अतः पूरे क्रम में एक ही पैटर्न रहता है<br>इसलिए d, b, c, a रिक्त स्थान सही भरता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): dbca है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000071005","section":"REASONING","topic":"Figure Series & Figure Analogy","question":{"en":"Select a figure from amongst the alternatives that will continue the same series as established by the Problem Figures.<br><b>Problem Figures:</b><br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q25.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"उन विकल्पों में से आकृति चुनिए जो प्रश्न आकृतियों द्वारा स्थापित उसी श्रेणी को आगे बढ़ाएगी।<br><b>प्रश्न आकृतियाँ:</b><br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q25.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{},"2":{},"3":{},"4":{}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"In the first figure there are four half-shaded circles around the diamond, in the second three and in the third two, so one half-shaded circle is removed at every step<br>At the same time the remaining half-shaded circle travels along the edge towards the top-right corner, while the small hollow circle stays at the centre of the diamond<br>In the next figure only one half-shaded circle is left, sitting just outside the top-right corner with the hollow circle in the middle, which is option 4<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q25_opt4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\">.</b>","hi":"पहली आकृति में हीरे के चारों ओर चार आधे-छायांकित वृत्त, दूसरी में तीन और तीसरी में दो हैं, अतः प्रत्येक चरण में एक आधा-छायांकित वृत्त हटता है<br>साथ ही शेष आधा-छायांकित वृत्त किनारे के साथ ऊपर-दाएँ कोने की ओर बढ़ता है और छोटा खोखला वृत्त हीरे के केंद्र पर बना रहता है<br>अगली आकृति में केवल एक आधा-छायांकित वृत्त ऊपर-दाएँ कोने के ठीक बाहर तथा खोखला वृत्त मध्य में होगा, जो विकल्प 4 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): <img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q25_opt4.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q25.jpg"],"options":{"1":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q25_opt1.jpg"],"2":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q25_opt2.jpg"],"3":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q25_opt3.jpg"],"4":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q25_opt4.jpg"]},"solution":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q25_opt4.jpg"]}}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000071006","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Part 1 and Part 2 of the Constitution","question":{"en":"What does the First Schedule of the Indian Constitution contain? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान की पहली अनुसूची में क्या सम्मिलित है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"State names","hi":"राज्यों के नाम"},"2":{"en":"Oath forms","hi":"शपथ के प्रारूप"},"3":{"en":"Salary scales","hi":"वेतनमान"},"4":{"en":"Rajya Sabha","hi":"राज्यसभा"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – State names</b><br>The <b>First Schedule</b> of the Constitution contains the <b>names of the States and Union Territories</b> of India and the territories comprised in them. It is read with Articles 1 and 4, which deal with the Union and its territory.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Second Schedule deals with the <b>emoluments of the President, Governors, judges and the CAG</b>, and the Third Schedule contains the <b>forms of oath</b>.<br>• The Fourth Schedule allocates seats in the <b>Rajya Sabha</b> to states and union territories, and the Fifth and Sixth Schedules deal with scheduled areas and tribal areas.<br>• The Seventh Schedule contains the <b>Union, State and Concurrent Lists</b>, and the Eighth Schedule lists the 22 recognised languages.<br>• There are <b>12 Schedules</b> in the Constitution; the Ninth Schedule was added by the First Amendment (1951) and protects land reform laws from judicial review.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – राज्यों के नाम</b><br>संविधान की <b>पहली अनुसूची</b> में भारत के <b>राज्यों व केंद्रशासित प्रदेशों के नाम</b> तथा उनमें सम्मिलित राज्यक्षेत्र दिए गए हैं। इसे अनुच्छेद 1 व 4 के साथ पढ़ा जाता है, जो संघ व उसके राज्यक्षेत्र से संबंधित हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• दूसरी अनुसूची <b>राष्ट्रपति, राज्यपालों, न्यायाधीशों व CAG के पारिश्रमिक</b> से संबंधित है, तथा तीसरी अनुसूची में <b>शपथ के प्रारूप</b> हैं।<br>• चौथी अनुसूची राज्यों व केंद्रशासित प्रदेशों को <b>राज्यसभा</b> में स्थान आवंटित करती है, तथा पाँचवीं व छठी अनुसूचियाँ अनुसूचित क्षेत्रों व जनजातीय क्षेत्रों से संबंधित हैं।<br>• सातवीं अनुसूची में <b>संघ, राज्य व समवर्ती सूचियाँ</b> हैं, तथा आठवीं अनुसूची में 22 मान्यता प्राप्त भाषाएँ सूचीबद्ध हैं।<br>• संविधान में <b>12 अनुसूचियाँ</b> हैं; नौवीं अनुसूची पहले संशोधन (1951) से जोड़ी गई और भूमि सुधार विधियों को न्यायिक पुनर्विलोकन से संरक्षण देती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000071007","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Centre-State Relations","question":{"en":"Which Commission was appointed to examine Center-State relations in <b>1983</b>? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"<b>1983</b> में केंद्र-राज्य संबंधों की जाँच हेतु कौन-सा आयोग नियुक्त किया गया? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The Sarkaria Commission","hi":"सरकारिया आयोग"},"2":{"en":"The Mandal Commission","hi":"मंडल आयोग"},"3":{"en":"The Kothari Commission","hi":"कोठारी आयोग"},"4":{"en":"The Shah Commission","hi":"शाह आयोग"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – The Sarkaria Commission</b><br>The <b>Sarkaria Commission</b> was appointed in <b>1983</b> under the chairmanship of Justice R.S. Sarkaria to examine the <b>centre-state relations</b> in India and recommend changes within the framework of the Constitution. It submitted its report in 1988.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Its key recommendations included the appointment of <b>inter-state councils</b>, consultation with states in the appointment of Governors and restraint in the use of Article 356.<br>• <b>Mandal Commission (1979)</b> dealt with reservations for socially and educationally backward classes, and the <b>Kothari Commission (1964)</b> with education.<br>• The <b>Shah Commission (1977)</b> inquired into the excesses during the Emergency, while the Rajamannar Committee (1969) and the Punchhi Commission (2007) also examined centre-state relations.<br>• The <b>Inter-State Council</b> was set up in 1990 on the recommendation of the Sarkaria Commission under Article 263.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – सरकारिया आयोग</b><br><b>सरकारिया आयोग</b> <b>1983</b> में न्यायमूर्ति आर.एस. सरकारिया की अध्यक्षता में भारत में <b>केंद्र-राज्य संबंधों</b> की जाँच तथा संविधान के ढाँचे में सुधारों की सिफारिश हेतु नियुक्त किया गया। इसने 1988 में रिपोर्ट प्रस्तुत की।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसकी प्रमुख सिफारिशों में <b>अंतर-राज्य परिषदों</b> का गठन, राज्यपालों की नियुक्ति में राज्यों से परामर्श तथा अनुच्छेद 356 के प्रयोग में संयम सम्मिलित थे।<br>• <b>मंडल आयोग (1979)</b> सामाजिक व शैक्षिक रूप से पिछड़े वर्गों के आरक्षण से, तथा <b>कोठारी आयोग (1964)</b> शिक्षा से संबंधित था।<br>• <b>शाह आयोग (1977)</b> आपातकाल की अधिकताओं की जाँच हेतु बना, जबकि राजमन्नार समिति (1969) व पुंछी आयोग (2007) ने भी केंद्र-राज्य संबंधों पर विचार किया।<br>• सरकारिया आयोग की सिफारिश पर 1990 में अनुच्छेद 263 के अंतर्गत <b>अंतर-राज्य परिषद</b> गठित हुई।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000071008","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Himalayan River System","question":{"en":"Which river in India is notorious for the frequent shifting of its course, often causing devastating floods in the state of Bihar? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत की कौन-सी नदी अपने मार्ग के बार-बार बदलने हेतु कुख्यात है, जिससे बिहार राज्य में अकसर विनाशकारी बाढ़ आती है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ganga","hi":"गंगा"},"2":{"en":"Kosi","hi":"कोसी"},"3":{"en":"Damodar","hi":"दामोदर"},"4":{"en":"Brahmaputra","hi":"ब्रह्मपुत्र"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Kosi</b><br>The <b>Kosi</b> river is called the <b>\"Sorrow of Bihar\"</b> because it shifts its course frequently — by as much as 100 km over a century — and causes devastating floods in north Bihar. It carries a very heavy silt load from the Himalayas and deposits it on the plains, choking its channels.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Kosi rises in Tibet and Nepal and is formed by seven streams in Nepal (the \"Sapta Kosi\"); it joins the Ganga near <b>Kursela in Bihar</b>.<br>• Its flood control is managed by embankments built after the <b>Kosi Agreement of 1954 with Nepal</b>, and the river is known as the \"River of Sorrow\".<br>• The <b>Damodar</b> was called the \"Sorrow of Bengal\", and the Brahmaputra causes floods in Assam through braided channels and bank erosion.<br>• The Kosi is an antecedent river and flows through a gorge in the Himalayan region, entering the plain at Chatra in Nepal.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – कोसी</b><br><b>कोसी</b> नदी को <b>\"बिहार का शोक\"</b> कहा जाता है, क्योंकि यह अपना मार्ग बार-बार बदलती है — एक शताब्दी में लगभग 100 किमी तक — और उत्तर बिहार में विनाशकारी बाढ़ लाती है। यह हिमालय से बहुत अधिक गाद लाती है और मैदान में उसे जमा कर देती है, जिससे उसके मार्ग अवरुद्ध हो जाते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• कोसी तिब्बत व नेपाल में निकलती है और नेपाल में सात धाराओं (\"सप्त कोसी\") से बनती है; यह बिहार में <b>कुरसेला</b> के निकट गंगा में मिलती है।<br>• इसका बाढ़ नियंत्रण <b>1954 के कोसी समझौते (नेपाल के साथ)</b> के बाद बने तटबंधों से होता है, और इसे \"शोक नदी\" कहा जाता है।<br>• <b>दामोदर</b> को \"बंगाल का शोक\" कहा जाता था, और ब्रह्मपुत्र असम में गुंफित धाराओं तथा तट-अपरदन से बाढ़ लाती है।<br>• कोसी एक पूर्ववर्ती (antecedent) नदी है, जो हिमालयी क्षेत्र में गॉर्ज से बहकर नेपाल में चातरा के निकट मैदान में प्रवेश करती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000071009","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Supreme Court and High Court","question":{"en":"Which Article under the Indian Constitution lays down the establishment and composition of the Supreme Court? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के अंतर्गत कौन-सा अनुच्छेद सर्वोच्च न्यायालय की स्थापना व गठन का प्रावधान करता है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 123","hi":"अनुच्छेद 123"},"2":{"en":"Article 124","hi":"अनुच्छेद 124"},"3":{"en":"Article 125","hi":"अनुच्छेद 125"},"4":{"en":"Article 126","hi":"अनुच्छेद 126"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Article 124</b><br><b>Article 124</b> establishes the <b>Supreme Court of India</b> and lays down its composition — a Chief Justice of India and such number of other judges as Parliament may by law determine (34 at present).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Article 125</b> deals with the salaries and allowances of Supreme Court judges, and <b>Article 126</b> with the appointment of an <b>acting Chief Justice</b>.<br>• <b>Article 123</b> gives the President the power to promulgate ordinances; it has nothing to do with the Supreme Court.<br>• The Supreme Court’s jurisdiction is dealt with in Articles <b>131 to 136</b>, and Article 137 gives it the power to review its own judgments.<br>• The Supreme Court is the guardian of the Constitution and has the power of <b>judicial review</b> under Articles 13, 32 and 226; Article 32 is called the \"heart and soul\" of the Constitution by Dr. Ambedkar.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अनुच्छेद 124</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 124</b> <b>भारत के सर्वोच्च न्यायालय</b> की स्थापना करता है तथा उसका गठन निर्धारित करता है — भारत के मुख्य न्यायाधीश तथा संसद द्वारा विधि से निर्धारित अन्य न्यायाधीश (वर्तमान में 34)।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 125</b> सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के न्यायाधीशों के वेतन व भत्तों से तथा <b>अनुच्छेद 126</b> <b>कार्यवाहक मुख्य न्यायाधीश</b> की नियुक्ति से संबंधित है।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 123</b> राष्ट्रपति को अध्यादेश जारी करने की शक्ति देता है; इसका सर्वोच्च न्यायालय से कोई संबंध नहीं।<br>• सर्वोच्च न्यायालय का अधिकारक्षेत्र <b>अनुच्छेद 131 से 136</b> में है, तथा अनुच्छेद 137 उसे अपने निर्णयों के पुनर्विलोकन की शक्ति देता है।<br>• सर्वोच्च न्यायालय संविधान का संरक्षक है और अनुच्छेद 13, 32 व 226 के अंतर्गत <b>न्यायिक पुनर्विलोकन</b> की शक्ति रखता है; डॉ. आंबेडकर ने अनुच्छेद 32 को संविधान की \"आत्मा\" कहा था।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000071010","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Centre-State Relations","question":{"en":"Which Article of the Indian Constitution provides for the resolution of disputes concerning inter-state river waters? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान का कौन-सा अनुच्छेद अंतर-राज्यीय नदी जल से संबंधित विवादों के समाधान का प्रावधान करता है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 255","hi":"अनुच्छेद 255"},"2":{"en":"Article 260","hi":"अनुच्छेद 260"},"3":{"en":"Article 262","hi":"अनुच्छेद 262"},"4":{"en":"Article 265","hi":"अनुच्छेद 265"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Article 262</b><br><b>Article 262</b> provides that Parliament may by law provide for the adjudication of any <b>dispute or complaint with respect to the use, distribution or control of the waters of inter-state rivers or river valleys</b>, and may also exclude the jurisdiction of all courts, including the Supreme Court, in such matters.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Parliament enacted the <b>Inter-State River Water Disputes Act, 1956</b> under Article 262, under which tribunals have been set up for the Krishna, Godavari, Narmada, Cauvery and Ravi-Beas waters.<br>• Article 262 is in <b>Part XI (Relations between the Union and the States)</b>; the Cauvery dispute was adjudicated by a tribunal set up under the Act and later modified by the Supreme Court.<br>• <b>Article 265</b> prohibits taxation without the authority of law, and <b>Article 255</b> deals with the requirement of prior assent for certain state bills.<br>• The <b>Inter-State River Water Disputes (Amendment) Bill</b> proposes a single standing tribunal with benches to speed up settlements.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – अनुच्छेद 262</b><br><b>अनुच्छेद 262</b> का प्रावधान है कि संसद विधि द्वारा <b>अंतर-राज्यीय नदियों या नदी घाटियों के जल के उपयोग, वितरण या नियंत्रण के संबंध में किसी विवाद या शिकायत के न्यायनिर्णयन</b> का प्रावधान कर सकती है, और ऐसे मामलों में सर्वोच्च न्यायालय सहित सभी न्यायालयों के अधिकारक्षेत्र को बाहर भी कर सकती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अनुच्छेद 262 के अंतर्गत संसद ने <b>अंतर-राज्यीय नदी जल विवाद अधिनियम, 1956</b> बनाया, जिसके अंतर्गत कृष्णा, गोदावरी, नर्मदा, कावेरी व रावी-ब्यास जल हेतु न्यायाधिकरण बने।<br>• अनुच्छेद 262 <b>भाग XI (संघ व राज्यों के बीच संबंध)</b> में है; कावेरी विवाद अधिनियम के अंतर्गत गठित न्यायाधिकरण द्वारा निपटाया गया और बाद में सर्वोच्च न्यायालय ने उसमें संशोधन किया।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 265</b> विधि के प्राधिकार के बिना कराधान का निषेध करता है, तथा <b>अनुच्छेद 255</b> कुछ राज्य विधेयकों हेतु पूर्व स्वीकृति की अपेक्षा से संबंधित है।<br>• <b>अंतर-राज्यीय नदी जल विवाद (संशोधन) विधेयक</b> शीघ्र निपटान हेतु पीठों सहित एक स्थायी न्यायाधिकरण का प्रस्ताव करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000071011","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Electricity","question":{"en":"Which of the following is equivalent to the SI unit of electrical resistance? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा विद्युत प्रतिरोध के SI मात्रक के तुल्य है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Joule/Coulomb","hi":"जूल/कूलॉम"},"2":{"en":"Volt/Ampere","hi":"वोल्ट/ऐम्पियर"},"3":{"en":"Ampere/Volt","hi":"ऐम्पियर/वोल्ट"},"4":{"en":"Coulomb/Joule","hi":"कूलॉम/जूल"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Volt/Ampere</b><br>The SI unit of electrical resistance is the <b>ohm</b>, and since \\(R = \\frac{V}{I}\\), one ohm equals <b>one volt per ampere</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Joule/Coulomb</b> is the volt (unit of potential difference), and <b>Ampere/Volt</b> is the reciprocal — the siemens (unit of conductance).<br>• Ohm’s law states that \\(V = IR\\) at constant temperature; resistance depends on length, area, material and temperature: \\(R = \\rho \\frac{l}{A}\\).<br>• The unit of charge is the coulomb, of current the ampere, of power the watt and of energy the joule.<br>• A resistor’s resistance increases with length and decreases with the area of cross-section; resistivity is a property of the material.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – वोल्ट/ऐम्पियर</b><br>विद्युत प्रतिरोध का SI मात्रक <b>ओम</b> है, और चूँकि \\(R = \\frac{V}{I}\\), एक ओम = <b>एक वोल्ट प्रति ऐम्पियर</b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>जूल/कूलॉम</b> वोल्ट (विभवांतर का मात्रक) है, तथा <b>ऐम्पियर/वोल्ट</b> इसका व्युत्क्रम — साइमेंस (चालकता का मात्रक) है।<br>• ओम के नियमानुसार स्थिर ताप पर \\(V = IR\\); प्रतिरोध लंबाई, क्षेत्रफल, पदार्थ व ताप पर निर्भर करता है: \\(R = \\rho \\frac{l}{A}\\)।<br>• आवेश का मात्रक कूलॉम, धारा का ऐम्पियर, शक्ति का वाट तथा ऊर्जा का जूल है।<br>• प्रतिरोध लंबाई के साथ बढ़ता व अनुप्रस्थ काट के क्षेत्रफल के साथ घटता है; प्रतिरोधकता पदार्थ का गुण है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000071012","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Earth's Interior and Plate Tectonics & Latitude and Longitude","question":{"en":"What is the approximate equatorial circumference of the Earth? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पृथ्वी की भूमध्यरेखीय परिधि लगभग कितनी है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"20,000 km","hi":"20,000 किमी"},"2":{"en":"30,000 km","hi":"30,000 किमी"},"3":{"en":"40,000 km","hi":"40,000 किमी"},"4":{"en":"50,000 km","hi":"50,000 किमी"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 40,000 km</b><br>The equatorial circumference of the Earth is about <b>40,075 km</b>, which is commonly rounded to <b>40,000 km</b>. This is why one degree of longitude at the equator measures about 111 km.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Earth’s equatorial diameter is about <b>12,756 km</b> and the polar diameter about 12,714 km, so the Earth is an <b>oblate spheroid</b> flattened at the poles.<br>• The polar circumference is slightly less, about 40,008 km, because of the flattening at the poles.<br>• Latitude and longitude are measured in degrees, minutes and seconds, with <b>360 meridians</b> and 180 parallels; the equator is 0° latitude.<br>• The Earth’s rotation causes the <b>equatorial bulge</b>, and the length of one degree of latitude is about 111 km everywhere.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 40,000 किमी</b><br>पृथ्वी की भूमध्यरेखीय परिधि लगभग <b>40,075 किमी</b> है, जिसे सामान्यतः <b>40,000 किमी</b> माना जाता है। इसी कारण भूमध्य रेखा पर देशांतर का एक अंश लगभग 111 किमी होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पृथ्वी का भूमध्यरेखीय व्यास लगभग <b>12,756 किमी</b> तथा ध्रुवीय व्यास लगभग 12,714 किमी है, अतः पृथ्वी ध्रुवों पर चपटा <b>दीर्घवृत्ताभ (ओब्लेट स्फेरॉइड)</b> है।<br>• ध्रुवों पर चपटेपन के कारण ध्रुवीय परिधि कुछ कम, लगभग 40,008 किमी है।<br>• अक्षांश व देशांतर अंश, मिनट व सेकंड में मापे जाते हैं; <b>360 देशांतर रेखाएँ</b> तथा 180 अक्षांश रेखाएँ होती हैं; भूमध्य रेखा 0° अक्षांश है।<br>• पृथ्वी के घूर्णन से <b>भूमध्यरेखीय उभार</b> बनता है, तथा अक्षांश के एक अंश की लंबाई सर्वत्र लगभग 111 किमी है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000071013","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Minerals","question":{"en":"Which of the following is a major manganese mining area in Odisha? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से ओडिशा का प्रमुख मैंगनीज़ खनन क्षेत्र कौन-सा है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Gangpur","hi":"गंगपुर"},"2":{"en":"Rourkela","hi":"राउरकेला"},"3":{"en":"Cuttack","hi":"कटक"},"4":{"en":"Chitradurg","hi":"चित्रदुर्ग"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Gangpur</b><br><b>Gangpur</b> in Sundargarh district of Odisha is a major <b>manganese mining area</b>. Odisha is the <b>largest producer of manganese ore</b> in India, and its main manganese belts are Gangpur, Keonjhar, Koraput, Bolangir and Sundargarh.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Rourkela</b> is famous for its steel plant, <b>Cuttack</b> is a city and former capital, and <b>Chitradurga</b> is in Karnataka and known for its fort and mineral deposits.<br>• Manganese is used mainly in <b>steel making</b> (as a deoxidiser and alloy), in dry cells and in ferro-manganese; India has large reserves in Odisha, Karnataka, Madhya Pradesh and Maharashtra.<br>• Odisha also leads in the production of <b>iron ore, chromite, bauxite and coal</b> among Indian states.<br>• The <b>Barbil–Joda belt</b> in Keonjhar and the Bailadila mines in Chhattisgarh are major iron ore areas, while chromite comes from Sukinda in Odisha.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – गंगपुर</b><br>ओडिशा के सुंदरगढ़ जिले में <b>गंगपुर</b> एक प्रमुख <b>मैंगनीज़ खनन क्षेत्र</b> है। ओडिशा भारत में <b>मैंगनीज़ अयस्क का सर्वाधिक उत्पादक</b> राज्य है, और इसकी मुख्य मैंगनीज़ पट्टियाँ गंगपुर, क्योंझर, कोरापुट, बोलांगीर व सुंदरगढ़ हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>राउरकेला</b> अपने इस्पात संयंत्र हेतु प्रसिद्ध है, <b>कटक</b> एक नगर व पूर्व राजधानी है, तथा <b>चित्रदुर्ग</b> कर्नाटक में है और अपने किले व खनिज निक्षेपों हेतु जाना जाता है।<br>• मैंगनीज़ मुख्यतः <b>इस्पात निर्माण</b> (विऑक्सीकारक व मिश्रधातु के रूप में), शुष्क सेल तथा फेरो-मैंगनीज़ में प्रयुक्त होता है; भारत में बड़े भंडार ओडिशा, कर्नाटक, मध्य प्रदेश व महाराष्ट्र में हैं।<br>• ओडिशा <b>लौह अयस्क, क्रोमाइट, बॉक्साइट व कोयला</b> के उत्पादन में भी अग्रणी है।<br>• क्योंझर की <b>बारबिल–जोडा पट्टी</b> तथा छत्तीसगढ़ की बैलाडीला खानें प्रमुख लौह अयस्क क्षेत्र हैं, जबकि क्रोमाइट ओडिशा के सुकिंडा से आता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000071014","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Music and Musical Instruments","question":{"en":"Consider the following pairs of folk music traditions/ballads and their corresponding states:<br>1. Jammukula – Manipur<br>2. Baans Geet – Chhattisgarh<br>Which of the pairs given above is/are <b>correctly</b> matched? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"लोक संगीत परंपराओं/गाथाओं तथा उनके संबंधित राज्यों के निम्नलिखित युग्मों पर विचार कीजिए:<br>1. जम्मुकुला – मणिपुर<br>2. बांस गीत – छत्तीसगढ़<br>उपर्युक्त युग्मों में से कौन-सा/से <b>सही</b> सुमेलित है/हैं? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 only","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"2 only","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"Both 1 and 2","hi":"1 और 2 दोनों"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2","hi":"न 1, न ही 2"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – 2 only</b><br>Pair 2 is correct — <b>Baans Geet</b> (bamboo song) is a folk music tradition of <b>Chhattisgarh</b>, sung by the Baiga and other tribal communities with bamboo flutes and instruments. Pair 1 is incorrect, because <b>Jammukula</b> is a folk ballad tradition of <b>Chhattisgarh</b> (Bastar region) and not of Manipur.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Chhattisgarh’s folk traditions include <b>Pandavani, Jammukula, Baans Geet, Karma and Sohar</b>, sung in Chhattisgarhi and tribal languages.<br>• Manipur’s folk music includes the <b>Khullang Eshei</b> and the <b>Thang-ta</b> martial arts music; its classical form is the <b>Ras Leela</b> and Natya Sangeet.<br>• Folk ballads of India include <b>Pandavani</b> (Chhattisgarh), Maand (Rajasthan), Alha (Bundelkhand) and Villu Pattu (Tamil Nadu).<br>• The Baiga tribe lives in the forests of Madhya Pradesh and Chhattisgarh, and their songs are associated with the Karma festival.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – केवल 2</b><br>युग्म 2 सही है — <b>बांस गीत</b> <b>छत्तीसगढ़</b> की लोक संगीत परंपरा है, जिसे बैगा व अन्य जनजातीय समुदाय बाँस की बाँसुरी व वाद्यों के साथ गाते हैं। युग्म 1 गलत है, क्योंकि <b>जम्मुकुला</b> <b>छत्तीसगढ़</b> (बस्तर क्षेत्र) की लोक-गाथा परंपरा है, मणिपुर की नहीं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• छत्तीसगढ़ की लोक परंपराओं में <b>पंडवानी, जम्मुकुला, बांस गीत, कर्मा व सोहर</b> सम्मिलित हैं, जो छत्तीसगढ़ी व जनजातीय भाषाओं में गाए जाते हैं।<br>• मणिपुर के लोक संगीत में <b>खुल्लांग एशेई</b> तथा <b>थांग-ता</b> युद्धकला संगीत आते हैं; इसका शास्त्रीय रूप <b>रास लीला</b> व नाट्य संगीत है।<br>• भारत की लोक-गाथाओं में <b>पंडवानी</b> (छत्तीसगढ़), मांड (राजस्थान), आल्हा (बुंदेलखंड) तथा विल्लु पाट्टु (तमिलनाडु) सम्मिलित हैं।<br>• बैगा जनजाति मध्य प्रदेश व छत्तीसगढ़ के वनों में रहती है और उनके गीत कर्मा पर्व से जुड़े हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000071015","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"The government has a target to create 6 crore Lakhpati Didis. To fast-track this goal, which Ministry launched the National Campaign on Entrepreneurship in January 2026 in India? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"सरकार का 6 करोड़ लखपति दीदी बनाने का लक्ष्य है। इस लक्ष्य को तेज़ी से प्राप्त करने हेतु भारत में जनवरी 2026 में किस मंत्रालय ने राष्ट्रीय उद्यमिता अभियान शुरू किया? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ministry of Finance","hi":"वित्त मंत्रालय"},"2":{"en":"Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare","hi":"कृषि एवं किसान कल्याण मंत्रालय"},"3":{"en":"Ministry of Rural Development","hi":"ग्रामीण विकास मंत्रालय"},"4":{"en":"Ministry of Women and Child Development","hi":"महिला एवं बाल विकास मंत्रालय"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Ministry of Rural Development</b><br>On <b>12 January 2026</b> the <b>Ministry of Rural Development</b> launched the <b>National Campaign on Entrepreneurship</b> to strengthen rural women-led enterprises and accelerate the <b>Lakhpati Didi</b> initiative, with a plan to train 50,000 Community Resource Persons and 50 lakh SHG members under DAY-NRLM.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• A <b>Lakhpati Didi</b> is a Self-Help Group member whose household earns more than <b>₹1 lakh a year</b> from sustainable livelihood activities; the government’s target is 6 crore such women.<br>• The campaign is implemented under the <b>Deendayal Antyodaya Yojana – National Rural Livelihoods Mission (DAY-NRLM)</b> and builds on the Start-up Village Entrepreneurship Programme.<br>• Digital tools such as the <b>LokOS app and Digital Aajeevika Register</b> track the real-time income data of potential Lakhpati Didis.<br>• The Lakhpati Didi scheme was announced in the 2023 Independence Day address, and a separate <b>Drone Didi</b> component trains women to use drones in agriculture.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – ग्रामीण विकास मंत्रालय</b><br><b>12 जनवरी 2026</b> को <b>ग्रामीण विकास मंत्रालय</b> ने ग्रामीण महिला-नेतृत्व वाले उद्यमों को सशक्त करने तथा <b>लखपति दीदी</b> पहल को तेज़ करने हेतु <b>राष्ट्रीय उद्यमिता अभियान</b> शुरू किया, जिसके अंतर्गत DAY-NRLM के तहत 50,000 सामुदायिक संसाधन व्यक्तियों तथा 50 लाख स्वयं सहायता समूह सदस्यों को प्रशिक्षित करने की योजना है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>लखपति दीदी</b> वह स्वयं सहायता समूह सदस्य है जिसके परिवार की वार्षिक आय सतत आजीविका गतिविधियों से <b>₹1 लाख से अधिक</b> होती है; सरकार का लक्ष्य 6 करोड़ ऐसी महिलाएँ हैं।<br>• अभियान <b>दीनदयाल अंत्योदय योजना – राष्ट्रीय ग्रामीण आजीविका मिशन (DAY-NRLM)</b> के अंतर्गत क्रियान्वित होता है तथा स्टार्ट-अप विलेज एंटरप्रेन्योरशिप कार्यक्रम पर आधारित है।<br>• <b>LokOS ऐप व डिजिटल आजीविका रजिस्टर</b> जैसे डिजिटल साधन संभावित लखपति दीदियों की आय का वास्तविक समय आँकड़ा दर्ज करते हैं।<br>• लखपति दीदी योजना की घोषणा 2023 के स्वतंत्रता दिवस संबोधन में हुई थी, तथा अलग <b>ड्रोन दीदी</b> घटक महिलाओं को कृषि में ड्रोन के प्रयोग का प्रशिक्षण देता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000071016","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: MoUs and Agreements","question":{"en":"Under the Chabahar International Transport and Transit Corridor Agreement, how are decisions of the Coordination Council made? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"चाबहार अंतर्राष्ट्रीय परिवहन एवं पारगमन कॉरिडोर समझौते के अंतर्गत समन्वय परिषद के निर्णय कैसे लिए जाते हैं? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"By a simple majority vote","hi":"साधारण बहुमत मत से"},"2":{"en":"By a two-thirds majority vote","hi":"दो-तिहाई बहुमत मत से"},"3":{"en":"By consensus among all Contracting Parties","hi":"सभी संविदाकारी पक्षों के बीच सहमति से"},"4":{"en":"By the decision of the Chairperson alone","hi":"केवल अध्यक्ष के निर्णय से"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – By consensus among all Contracting Parties</b><br>Under the <b>Chabahar International Transport and Transit Corridor Agreement</b>, signed by <b>India, Iran and Afghanistan</b> in 2016, decisions of the <b>Coordination Council are taken by consensus among all Contracting Parties</b>, so that no member can be overruled on corridor matters.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The agreement tripartite in nature was signed in May 2016 during Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s visit to Tehran; India committed to develop the <b>Shahid Beheshti terminal at Chabahar port</b>.<br>• Chabahar gives India access to Afghanistan and Central Asia <b>bypassing Pakistan</b> and links to the International North-South Transport Corridor.<br>• <b>India Ports Global Limited (IPGL)</b> operates the Shahid Beheshti terminal, and the port connects to the Zaranj–Delaram highway in Afghanistan.<br>• The corridor supports trade in goods such as wheat, pulses and petroleum products and reduces transit time and cost to Central Asia.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – सभी संविदाकारी पक्षों के बीच सहमति से</b><br><b>चाबहार अंतर्राष्ट्रीय परिवहन एवं पारगमन कॉरिडोर समझौता</b>, जिसे <b>भारत, ईरान व अफगानिस्तान</b> ने 2016 में हस्ताक्षरित किया, के अंतर्गत <b>समन्वय परिषद के निर्णय सभी संविदाकारी पक्षों की सहमति</b> से लिए जाते हैं, ताकि कॉरिडोर के मामलों में किसी सदस्य पर निर्णय न थोपा जाए।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• यह त्रिपक्षीय समझौता मई 2016 में प्रधानमंत्री नरेंद्र मोदी की तेहरान यात्रा के दौरान हुआ; भारत ने <b>चाबहार बंदरगाह के शाहिद बेहेश्ती टर्मिनल</b> के विकास का दायित्व लिया।<br>• चाबहार भारत को <b>पाकिस्तान को दरकिनार करते हुए</b> अफगानिस्तान व मध्य एशिया तक पहुँच देता है और अंतर्राष्ट्रीय उत्तर-दक्षिण परिवहन कॉरिडोर से जुड़ता है।<br>• <b>इंडिया पोर्ट्स ग्लोबल लिमिटेड (IPGL)</b> शाहिद बेहेश्ती टर्मिनल का संचालन करता है तथा बंदरगाह अफगानिस्तान के जरंज–देलाराम मार्ग से जुड़ा है।<br>• कॉरिडोर गेहूँ, दालें व पेट्रोलियम उत्पादों के व्यापार में सहायक है और मध्य एशिया तक पारगमन समय व लागत घटाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000071017","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: World Map","question":{"en":"Which South Asian country is known as the “Land of Thunder Dragon”? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"कौन-सा दक्षिण एशियाई देश \"लैंड ऑफ द थंडर ड्रैगन\" के नाम से जाना जाता है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Bhutan","hi":"भूटान"},"2":{"en":"Maldives","hi":"मालदीव"},"3":{"en":"Bangladesh","hi":"बांग्लादेश"},"4":{"en":"Nepal","hi":"नेपाल"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Bhutan</b><br><b>Bhutan</b> is known as the <b>\"Land of the Thunder Dragon\"</b> — Druk Yul in Dzongkha — because of the violent thunderstorms that sweep down from the Himalayas. The dragon is the national symbol on its flag.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Bhutan is a landlocked Himalayan kingdom with Thimphu as its capital; its national flag is half orange and half yellow with a white dragon.<br>• Its economy is based on <b>hydropower</b> exports to India, agriculture and tourism; it is the world’s first carbon-negative country.<br>• Bhutan became a constitutional monarchy in <b>2008</b> and follows the philosophy of <b>Gross National Happiness</b>.<br>• Nepal is the \"Land of the Himalayas\", Bangladesh is the \"Land of Rivers\", and Maldives is the \"Land of a Thousand Islands\" — each with its own popular epithet.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – भूटान</b><br><b>भूटान</b> <b>\"लैंड ऑफ द थंडर ड्रैगन\"</b> — जोंगखा में द्रुक युल — के नाम से जाना जाता है, क्योंकि हिमालय से आने वाले प्रचंड तूफानों के कारण ऐसा कहा जाता है। ड्रैगन उसके ध्वज पर राष्ट्रीय प्रतीक है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भूटान हिमालयी स्थलरुद्ध राज्य है, जिसकी राजधानी थिम्पू है; इसका राष्ट्रीय ध्वज आधा नारंगी-आधा पीला है, जिस पर सफेद ड्रैगन है।<br>• इसकी अर्थव्यवस्था भारत को <b>जलविद्युत</b> निर्यात, कृषि व पर्यटन पर आधारित है; यह विश्व का पहला कार्बन-निगेटिव देश है।<br>• भूटान <b>2008</b> में संवैधानिक राजतंत्र बना तथा <b>सकल राष्ट्रीय प्रसन्नता</b> के दर्शन का पालन करता है।<br>• नेपाल \"हिमालय की भूमि\", बांग्लादेश \"नदियों की भूमि\" तथा मालदीव \"हज़ार द्वीपों की भूमि\" कहा जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000071018","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"A is attacked by a violent mob attempting to murder him. Young children are mixed within the mob. He can save himself only by firing into the crowd, though this creates risk to the children. A fire and one child die. Which of the following is correct under the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 in India? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"A पर हत्या के प्रयास हेतु एक उग्र भीड़ द्वारा आक्रमण होता है। भीड़ में छोटे बच्चे भी हैं। वह भीड़ पर गोली चलाकर ही अपनी रक्षा कर सकता है, यद्यपि इससे बच्चों को खतरा है। गोली चलती है और एक बच्चे की मृत्यु हो जाती है। भारत में भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023 के अंतर्गत निम्नलिखित में से कौन सही है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A is guilty because innocent persons can never be harmed in private defence.","hi":"A दोषी है, क्योंकि निजी प्रतिरक्षा में निर्दोष व्यक्तियों को कभी हानि नहीं पहुँचाई जा सकती।"},"2":{"en":"A is guilty because children were present.","hi":"A दोषी है, क्योंकि वहाँ बच्चे उपस्थित थे।"},"3":{"en":"A remains protected because private defence allows unavoidable risk in such assaults.","hi":"A संरक्षित रहेगा, क्योंकि ऐसे आक्रमणों में निजी प्रतिरक्षा अपरिहार्य जोखिम की अनुमति देती है।"},"4":{"en":"A is protected only if no innocent person is actually injured.","hi":"A केवल तभी संरक्षित है जब वास्तव में कोई निर्दोष व्यक्ति घायल न हो।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – A remains protected because private defence allows unavoidable risk in such assaults.</b><br>Under Section 34 of the <b>Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023</b> (the old Section 96 to 106 of the IPC), the right of <b>private defence</b> is available when a person is faced with an imminent attack. If the force used is proportionate and the risk to bystanders is unavoidable, the person acting in self-defence is <b>protected</b>; the harm caused to an innocent person in such a situation does not by itself make the act an offence.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Sections 34 to 44 of the BNS deal with the <b>right of private defence</b>, including its extent and when it extends to causing death.<br>• The defence is available only against an <b>unlawful aggression</b> and not against a lawful act, and the force must not be excessive.<br>• The right is available to protect one’s own body, the body of another person, and property against theft, robbery, mischief and house trespass.<br>• The <b>BNS, BNSS and BSA</b> replaced the IPC, CrPC and Indian Evidence Act with effect from 1 July 2024.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – A संरक्षित रहेगा, क्योंकि ऐसे आक्रमणों में निजी प्रतिरक्षा अपरिहार्य जोखिम की अनुमति देती है।</b><br><b>भारतीय न्याय संहिता, 2023 की धारा 34</b> (पूर्व IPC की धाराएँ 96 से 106) के अंतर्गत <b>निजी प्रतिरक्षा</b> का अधिकार तब उपलब्ध होता है जब व्यक्ति पर आसन्न आक्रमण हो। यदि प्रयुक्त बल समानुपाती हो तथा आसपास के व्यक्तियों को जोखिम अपरिहार्य हो, तो आत्मरक्षा करने वाला व्यक्ति <b>संरक्षित</b> रहता है; ऐसी स्थिति में निर्दोष व्यक्ति को हुई हानि मात्र से कार्य अपराध नहीं बनता।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• BNS की धाराएँ 34 से 44 <b>निजी प्रतिरक्षा के अधिकार</b> से संबंधित हैं, जिसमें उसकी सीमा तथा वह स्थिति जहाँ यह मृत्यु तक कारित करने की अनुमति देती है, सम्मिलित है।<br>• यह प्रतिरक्षा केवल <b>अविधिक आक्रमण</b> के विरुद्ध उपलब्ध है, किसी विधिपूर्ण कार्य के विरुद्ध नहीं, तथा बल अत्यधिक नहीं होना चाहिए।<br>• यह अधिकार अपने या अन्य के शरीर तथा चोरी, डकैती, उत्पात व गृह-अतिचार के विरुद्ध संपत्ति की रक्षा हेतु उपलब्ध है।<br>• <b>BNS, BNSS व BSA</b> ने 1 जुलाई 2024 से IPC, CrPC व भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम का स्थान लिया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000071019","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Appointments and Resignations","question":{"en":"Who has been appointed as the new Chairperson of the Central Board of Secondary Education (CBSE) in June 2026? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"जून 2026 में केंद्रीय माध्यमिक शिक्षा बोर्ड (CBSE) के नए अध्यक्ष के रूप में किसे नियुक्त किया गया? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lokhande Prashant Sitaram","hi":"लोखंडे प्रशांत सीताराम"},"2":{"en":"Himanshu Kumar Mishra","hi":"हिमांशु कुमार मिश्रा"},"3":{"en":"Manoj Kumar Srivastava","hi":"मनोज कुमार श्रीवास्तव"},"4":{"en":"Varun Bhardwaj","hi":"वरुण भारद्वाज"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Lokhande Prashant Sitaram</b><br><b>Lokhande Prashant Sitaram</b> was appointed <b>Chairperson of the CBSE in June 2026</b>. The post of CBSE chairperson is held by a senior officer of the Ministry of Education, and the Board functions under the Ministry of Education.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The CBSE is a <b>national level board of education</b> for public and private schools, with headquarters at New Delhi, and conducts the Class 10 and 12 board examinations and JEE Main.<br>• <b>Varun Bhardwaj</b> was appointed <b>Secretary of the CBSE</b> in 2026 (a 2008-batch Indian Information Service officer), not the Chairperson.<br>• The CBSE was formed in <b>1929</b> as the Board of High School and Intermediate Education and was reconstituted in 1952 and 1962.<br>• The Board’s responsibilities include prescribing the curriculum, conducting examinations and affiliating schools in India and abroad.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – लोखंडे प्रशांत सीताराम</b><br><b>लोखंडे प्रशांत सीताराम</b> को <b>जून 2026 में CBSE का अध्यक्ष</b> नियुक्त किया गया। CBSE अध्यक्ष का पद शिक्षा मंत्रालय के वरिष्ठ अधिकारी के पास होता है तथा बोर्ड शिक्षा मंत्रालय के अधीन कार्य करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• CBSE सार्वजनिक व निजी विद्यालयों हेतु <b>राष्ट्रीय स्तर का शिक्षा बोर्ड</b> है, जिसका मुख्यालय नई दिल्ली में है और जो कक्षा 10 व 12 की बोर्ड परीक्षाएँ तथा JEE मेन आयोजित करता है।<br>• <b>वरुण भारद्वाज</b> को 2026 में CBSE का <b>सचिव</b> नियुक्त किया गया (2008 बैच के भारतीय सूचना सेवा अधिकारी), अध्यक्ष नहीं।<br>• CBSE की स्थापना <b>1929</b> में बोर्ड ऑफ हाई स्कूल एंड इंटरमीडिएट एजुकेशन के रूप में हुई तथा 1952 व 1962 में इसका पुनर्गठन हुआ।<br>• बोर्ड के दायित्वों में पाठ्यक्रम निर्धारण, परीक्षा आयोजन तथा भारत व विदेश के विद्यालयों का संबद्धन सम्मिलित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000071020","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Awards and Honours","question":{"en":"Who won the <b>2025</b> Shakti Bhatt Prize for her debut memoir <i>The Lucky Ones</i>? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"<b>2025</b> का शक्ति भट्ट पुरस्कार अपनी पहली स्मृति-कृति <i>द लकी वन्स</i> हेतु किसने जीता? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Shubhangi Swarup","hi":"शुभांगी स्वरूप"},"2":{"en":"Zara Chowdhary","hi":"ज़ारा चौधरी"},"3":{"en":"Deepti Kapoor","hi":"दीप्ति कपूर"},"4":{"en":"Meena Kandasamy","hi":"मीना कंडसामी"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Zara Chowdhary</b><br><b>Zara Chowdhary</b> won the 2025 Shakti Bhatt Prize for her debut memoir <i>The Lucky Ones</i>, which recounts her experience as a <b>16-year-old during the 2002 Gujarat riots</b> in Ahmedabad. It was the final edition of the prize.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Shakti Bhatt Prize, instituted in <b>2008</b>, was awarded to debut writers from South Asia; the foundation discontinued the prize after 2025.<br>• It was set up in memory of the writer Shakti Bhatt by her husband, the poet <b>Jeet Thayil</b>, and her family.<br>• <b>Shubhangi Swarup</b> won for <i>Latitudes of Longing</i>, Deepti Kapoor for <i>Age of Vice</i> was shortlisted, and Meena Kandasamy is a poet and novelist.<br>• <i>The Lucky Ones</i> was published in 2024 and also won the <b>JCB Prize for Literature</b> in 2025.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – ज़ारा चौधरी</b><br><b>ज़ारा चौधरी</b> ने अपनी पहली स्मृति-कृति <i>द लकी वन्स</i> हेतु 2025 का शक्ति भट्ट पुरस्कार जीता, जिसमें अहमदाबाद में <b>2002 के गुजरात दंगों के समय 16 वर्ष की आयु</b> का उनका अनुभव वर्णित है। यह पुरस्कार का अंतिम संस्करण था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>2008</b> में आरंभ शक्ति भट्ट पुरस्कार दक्षिण एशिया के नए लेखकों को दिया जाता था; फाउंडेशन ने 2025 के बाद पुरस्कार बंद कर दिया।<br>• यह लेखिका शक्ति भट्ट की स्मृति में उनके पति, कवि <b>जीत थायल</b> तथा परिवार द्वारा स्थापित किया गया था।<br>• <b>शुभांगी स्वरूप</b> को <i>लैटिट्यूड्स ऑफ लॉन्गिंग</i> हेतु अवार्ड मिला, दीप्ति कपूर <i>एज ऑफ वाइस</i> हेतु लघुसूची में रहीं, तथा मीना कंडसामी कवयित्री व उपन्यासकार हैं।<br>• <i>द लकी वन्स</i> 2024 में प्रकाशित हुई और 2025 में इसे <b>JCB साहित्य पुरस्कार</b> भी मिला।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000071021","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"What is meant by disinvestment of public sector enterprises in India? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"भारत में सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र के उपक्रमों के विनिवेश का क्या अर्थ है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Merging two loss-making public sector companies","hi":"दो घाटे वाली सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र कंपनियों का विलय"},"2":{"en":"Nationalising a private sector company","hi":"निजी क्षेत्र की कंपनी का राष्ट्रीयकरण"},"3":{"en":"Selling off part of the equity of PSEs to the public","hi":"सार्वजनिक उपक्रमों की पूँजी का भाग जनता को बेचना"},"4":{"en":"Closing down a public sector enterprise permanently","hi":"सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र के उपक्रम को स्थायी रूप से बंद करना"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Selling off part of the equity of PSEs to the public</b><br><b>Disinvestment</b> means the <b>sale of a part of the government’s equity in public sector enterprises to the public, institutions or a strategic partner</b>, so as to raise resources, improve efficiency and widen shareholding. It does not amount to closing down the enterprise or nationalising a private company.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Disinvestment in India began with the <b>New Industrial Policy of 1991</b>; a separate Department of Disinvestment was set up in 1999, now the <b>Department of Investment and Public Asset Management (DIPAM)</b>, under the Ministry of Finance.<br>• Disinvestment may be <b>minority</b> (sale of less than 51%) or <b>strategic</b> (transfer of management control), as in the case of Air India.<br>• Proceeds go to the <b>National Investment Fund</b>, and the government aims to use them for capital expenditure in social and infrastructure sectors.<br>• The <b>New Public Sector Enterprise Policy (2021)</b> keeps public sector presence only in strategic sectors and aims for privatisation in non-strategic areas.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – सार्वजनिक उपक्रमों की पूँजी का भाग जनता को बेचना</b><br><b>विनिवेश</b> का अर्थ है <b>सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र के उपक्रमों में सरकार की पूँजी का एक भाग जनता, संस्थाओं या रणनीतिक साझेदार को बेचना</b>, जिससे संसाधन जुटें, दक्षता बढ़े और अंशधारिता का विस्तार हो। इसका अर्थ उपक्रम को बंद करना या निजी कंपनी का राष्ट्रीयकरण नहीं है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत में विनिवेश <b>1991 की नई औद्योगिक नीति</b> से आरंभ हुआ; 1999 में पृथक विनिवेश विभाग बना, जो अब वित्त मंत्रालय के अधीन <b>निवेश एवं लोक परिसंपत्ति प्रबंधन विभाग (DIPAM)</b> है।<br>• विनिवेश <b>अल्पांश</b> (51% से कम बिक्री) या <b>रणनीतिक</b> (प्रबंधन नियंत्रण हस्तांतरण) हो सकता है, जैसे एयर इंडिया में हुआ।<br>• प्राप्तियाँ <b>राष्ट्रीय निवेश कोष</b> में जाती हैं और सरकार इन्हें सामाजिक व अवसंरचना क्षेत्र के पूँजीगत व्यय हेतु प्रयोग करना चाहती है।<br>• <b>नई सार्वजनिक क्षेत्र उपक्रम नीति (2021)</b> सार्वजनिक उपस्थिति केवल रणनीतिक क्षेत्रों तक रखती है तथा गैर-रणनीतिक क्षेत्रों में निजीकरण का लक्ष्य रखती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000071022","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: Government Schemes and Policies (Current)","question":{"en":"Which planning approach is essential for ensuring sustainable development of heritage and tourism towns according to the Urban and Regional Development Plans Formulation and Implementation (URDPFI) Guidelines? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"शहरी एवं क्षेत्रीय विकास योजना निर्माण एवं क्रियान्वयन (URDPFI) दिशानिर्देशों के अनुसार विरासत व पर्यटन नगरों के सतत विकास हेतु कौन-सी योजना-पद्धति आवश्यक है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Military zoning","hi":"सैन्य ज़ोनिंग"},"2":{"en":"Carrying capacity evaluation","hi":"वहन क्षमता का मूल्यांकन"},"3":{"en":"Defence mapping","hi":"रक्षा मानचित्रण"},"4":{"en":"Export regulation","hi":"निर्यात नियमन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Carrying capacity evaluation</b><br>According to the <b>URDPFI Guidelines</b> of the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs, a <b>carrying capacity evaluation</b> is essential for heritage and tourism towns — it assesses the maximum number of visitors and activities an area can support without damaging its heritage, environment and infrastructure, and helps link tourism growth with conservation.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The URDPFI Guidelines (2015) provide the framework for preparing <b>perspective plans, development plans and local area plans</b> in urban and regional areas.<br>• Carrying capacity covers <b>physical, environmental, social and infrastructure capacity</b>, and is used to regulate tourist inflow to hill stations, coastal and heritage towns.<br>• The guidelines also emphasise <b>heritage conservation plans, special area plans</b> and participatory planning with urban local bodies.<br>• The Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs supports heritage cities through schemes such as the <b>HRIDAY scheme and the Swadesh Darshan and PRASHAD programmes</b> of tourism.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – वहन क्षमता का मूल्यांकन</b><br>आवास एवं शहरी कार्य मंत्रालय के <b>URDPFI दिशानिर्देशों</b> के अनुसार विरासत व पर्यटन नगरों हेतु <b>वहन क्षमता का मूल्यांकन</b> आवश्यक है — यह आँकता है कि कोई क्षेत्र अपनी विरासत, पर्यावरण व अवसंरचना को हानि पहुँचाए बिना कितने पर्यटक व गतिविधियाँ सहन कर सकता है, और पर्यटन वृद्धि को संरक्षण से जोड़ता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• URDPFI दिशानिर्देश (2015) शहरी व क्षेत्रीय क्षेत्रों में <b>परिप्रेक्ष्य योजना, विकास योजना व स्थानीय क्षेत्र योजना</b> बनाने का ढाँचा देते हैं।<br>• वहन क्षमता में <b>भौतिक, पर्यावरणीय, सामाजिक व अवसंरचना क्षमता</b> सम्मिलित होती है और इसका उपयोग पहाड़ी स्थलों, तटीय व विरासत नगरों में पर्यटकों के प्रवाह को नियंत्रित करने हेतु होता है।<br>• दिशानिर्देश <b>विरासत संरक्षण योजनाओं, विशेष क्षेत्र योजनाओं</b> तथा शहरी स्थानीय निकायों के साथ सहभागी योजना पर भी बल देते हैं।<br>• मंत्रालय <b>HRIDAY योजना</b> तथा पर्यटन मंत्रालय के स्वदेश दर्शन व प्रशाद कार्यक्रमों के माध्यम से विरासत नगरों को सहायता देता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000071023","section":"GK","topic":"Science and Technology: Science and Technology","question":{"en":"Which of the following is the first fully “Make-in-India” 32-bit microprocessor qualified for use in the harsh environmental conditions of launch vehicles, developed jointly by ISRO and the Semiconductor Laboratory in <b>2025</b>? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"<b>2025</b> में इसरो तथा अर्धचालक प्रयोगशाला द्वारा संयुक्त रूप से विकसित, प्रक्षेपण यानों की कठोर पर्यावरणीय परिस्थितियों में प्रयोग हेतु अर्हित, पहला पूर्णतः \"मेक-इन-इंडिया\" 32-बिट माइक्रोप्रोसेसर कौन-सा है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Vikram3201","hi":"विक्रम3201"},"2":{"en":"NavIC2000","hi":"नाविक2000"},"3":{"en":"Aryabhata32","hi":"आर्यभट32"},"4":{"en":"Rohini128","hi":"रोहिणी128"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Vikram3201</b><br><b>Vikram 3201</b> is the <b>first fully indigenous 32-bit microprocessor</b> qualified for use in the harsh environmental conditions of launch vehicles, developed jointly by ISRO’s <b>Vikram Sarabhai Space Centre</b> and the <b>Semiconductor Laboratory (SCL), Chandigarh</b> in 2025.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It was fabricated at SCL’s <b>180 nm CMOS semiconductor fab</b> and is an advanced version of the 16-bit <b>Vikram 1601</b> microprocessor used in ISRO’s launch vehicle avionics since 2009.<br>• Along with Vikram 3201, ISRO and SCL developed <b>Kalpana 3201</b>, a 32-bit SPARC V8 RISC microprocessor, and other devices such as a reconfigurable data acquisition system.<br>• The first production lots were handed over to the Secretary, Department of Space in March 2025, and the device was validated in the Mission Management Computer of <b>POEM-4 on PSLV-C60</b>.<br>• The software tools, including the Ada compiler and IDE, were developed in-house by ISRO, supporting the goal of <b>Atmanirbhar Bharat</b> in high-reliability electronics.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – विक्रम3201</b><br><b>विक्रम 3201</b> प्रक्षेपण यानों की कठोर पर्यावरणीय परिस्थितियों में प्रयोग हेतु अर्हित <b>पहला पूर्णतः स्वदेशी 32-बिट माइक्रोप्रोसेसर</b> है, जिसे 2025 में इसरो के <b>विक्रम साराभाई अंतरिक्ष केंद्र</b> तथा <b>अर्धचालक प्रयोगशाला (SCL), चंडीगढ़</b> ने संयुक्त रूप से विकसित किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसे SCL के <b>180 नैनोमीटर CMOS फैब</b> में बनाया गया और यह 2009 से इसरो के प्रक्षेपण यान एवियोनिक्स में प्रयुक्त 16-बिट <b>विक्रम 1601</b> का उन्नत संस्करण है।<br>• विक्रम 3201 के साथ इसरो व SCL ने <b>कल्पना 3201</b> (32-बिट SPARC V8 RISC माइक्रोप्रोसेसर) तथा पुन:संरूपणीय डेटा अधिग्रहण प्रणाली जैसे उपकरण भी विकसित किए।<br>• मार्च 2025 में पहले उत्पादन लॉट अंतरिक्ष विभाग के सचिव को सौंपे गए तथा उपकरण <b>PSLV-C60 के POEM-4</b> के मिशन मैनेजमेंट कंप्यूटर में सत्यापित हुआ।<br>• अदा कंपाइलर व IDE सहित सॉफ्टवेयर उपकरण इसरो ने स्वयं विकसित किए, जो उच्च-विश्वसनीयता इलेक्ट्रॉनिक्स में <b>आत्मनिर्भर भारत</b> के लक्ष्य को बल देते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000071024","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Five Year Plan and Industrial Policy Resolution","question":{"en":"Which of the following sectors was declared the \"prime moving force\" of the Indian economy under the Tenth Five-Year Plan (2002–2007)? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दसवीं पंचवर्षीय योजना (2002–2007) के अंतर्गत भारतीय अर्थव्यवस्था की \"प्रमुख प्रेरक शक्ति\" किस क्षेत्र को घोषित किया गया था? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Industrial sector","hi":"औद्योगिक क्षेत्र"},"2":{"en":"Agriculture sector","hi":"कृषि क्षेत्र"},"3":{"en":"Service sector","hi":"सेवा क्षेत्र"},"4":{"en":"External trade sector","hi":"बाह्य व्यापार क्षेत्र"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Agriculture sector</b><br>The Tenth Five-Year Plan (2002–2007) declared <b>agriculture</b> as the <b>\"prime moving force\" of the Indian economy</b> and set a target of 8% GDP growth with 4% growth in agriculture, along with doubling per capita income in ten years.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Tenth Plan focused on <b>agriculture, employment generation, poverty reduction and regional inequality</b>, and introduced monitorable social and economic targets.<br>• It followed the Ninth Plan (1997–2002), which emphasised \"Growth with Social Justice and Equality\" and was based on the Mahalanobis model.<br>• The <b>Eleventh Plan (2007–12)</b> aimed at \"Faster and More Inclusive Growth\" and the Twelfth Plan (2012–17) at \"Faster, More Inclusive and Sustainable Growth\".<br>• Agriculture contributes about <b>18% of India’s GVA</b> but employs over 45% of the workforce, so its growth remains central to poverty reduction.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – कृषि क्षेत्र</b><br>दसवीं पंचवर्षीय योजना (2002–2007) ने <b>कृषि</b> को <b>भारतीय अर्थव्यवस्था की \"प्रमुख प्रेरक शक्ति\"</b> घोषित किया तथा 8% GDP वृद्धि के लक्ष्य के साथ कृषि में 4% वृद्धि तथा दस वर्षों में प्रति व्यक्ति आय दोगुनी करने का लक्ष्य रखा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• दसवीं योजना का बल <b>कृषि, रोजगार सृजन, गरीबी न्यूनीकरण व क्षेत्रीय असमानता</b> पर था और इसमें निगरानी-योग्य सामाजिक व आर्थिक लक्ष्य रखे गए।<br>• इससे पहले नौवीं योजना (1997–2002) थी, जिसमें \"सामाजिक न्याय व समानता के साथ विकास\" पर बल था और वह महालनोबिस मॉडल पर आधारित थी।<br>• <b>ग्यारहवीं योजना (2007–12)</b> का लक्ष्य \"तीव्रतर व अधिक समावेशी विकास\" तथा बारहवीं योजना (2012–17) का \"तीव्रतर, अधिक समावेशी व सतत विकास\" था।<br>• कृषि भारत के GVA में लगभग <b>18%</b> का योगदान देती है परंतु 45% से अधिक कार्यबल को रोजगार देती है, अतः गरीबी घटाने में उसकी वृद्धि महत्वपूर्ण है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000071025","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Ecosystem","question":{"en":"Under what condition can renewable natural resources become depleted? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"किस स्थिति में नवीकरणीय प्राकृतिक संसाधन समाप्त हो सकते हैं? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Renewable natural resources regenerate only through artificial means.","hi":"नवीकरणीय प्राकृतिक संसाधन केवल कृत्रिम साधनों से पुनर्जीवित होते हैं।"},"2":{"en":"Population growth has no effect on renewable natural resources.","hi":"जनसंख्या वृद्धि का नवीकरणीय प्राकृतिक संसाधनों पर कोई प्रभाव नहीं होता।"},"3":{"en":"Human consumption of renewable natural resources may exceed their rate of natural regeneration.","hi":"नवीकरणीय प्राकृतिक संसाधनों की मानव खपत उनके प्राकृतिक पुनर्जनन की दर से अधिक हो सकती है।"},"4":{"en":"Renewable natural resources are immune to environmental degradation.","hi":"नवीकरणीय प्राकृतिक संसाधन पर्यावरणीय क्षरण से प्रतिरक्षित हैं।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Human consumption of renewable natural resources may exceed their rate of natural regeneration.</b><br>Renewable resources such as forests, fish, groundwater and soil are replenished by nature, but they become <b>depleted when the rate of human consumption exceeds the rate of natural regeneration</b>. Sustainable use therefore means keeping consumption within the regenerative capacity of the resource.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Examples of over-exploitation are <b>groundwater depletion</b> in north-west India, overfishing and deforestation beyond the rate of replanting.<br>• Resources are classified as <b>renewable, non-renewable and perpetual</b>; non-renewables such as coal and petroleum have a fixed stock.<br>• The concept of <b>sustainable development</b>, defined by the Brundtland Commission (1987), requires that resource use should not compromise the needs of future generations.<br>• <b>Ecological footprint</b> measures human demand on nature, and \"Earth Overshoot Day\" marks the date when annual demand exceeds what the planet can regenerate.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – नवीकरणीय प्राकृतिक संसाधनों की मानव खपत उनके प्राकृतिक पुनर्जनन की दर से अधिक हो सकती है।</b><br>वन, मत्स्य, भूजल व मृदा जैसे नवीकरणीय संसाधन प्रकृति द्वारा पुनः भरे जाते हैं, परंतु <b>जब मानव खपत की दर प्राकृतिक पुनर्जनन की दर से अधिक हो जाती है</b> तो वे समाप्त होने लगते हैं। अतः सतत उपयोग का अर्थ है खपत को संसाधन की पुनरुत्पादन क्षमता के भीतर रखना।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अति-दोहन के उदाहरण हैं — उत्तर-पश्चिम भारत में <b>भूजल का ह्रास</b>, अत्यधिक मत्स्यन तथा पुनर्रोपण दर से अधिक वनों की कटाई।<br>• संसाधन <b>नवीकरणीय, अनवीकरणीय व शाश्वत</b> में वर्गीकृत होते हैं; कोयला व पेट्रोलियम जैसे अनवीकरणीय संसाधनों का भंडार सीमित है।<br>• ब्रुंटलैंड आयोग (1987) द्वारा परिभाषित <b>सतत विकास</b> की अवधारणा के अनुसार संसाधन उपयोग भावी पीढ़ियों की आवश्यकताओं से समझौता नहीं करना चाहिए।<br>• <b>पारिस्थितिक पदचिह्न</b> प्रकृति पर मानव माँग को मापता है, तथा \"अर्थ ओवरशूट डे\" वह तिथि है जब वार्षिक माँग पृथ्वी की पुनरुत्पादन क्षमता से अधिक हो जाती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000071026","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Microeconomics","question":{"en":"Which of the following correctly distinguishes movement along a demand curve from a shift in the demand curve? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन माँग वक्र के अनुदिश गति तथा माँग वक्र के स्थानांतरण के बीच सही अंतर करता है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Both are caused only by price changes.","hi":"दोनों केवल कीमत परिवर्तन से होते हैं।"},"2":{"en":"Movement occurs due to income changes and shifts due to price changes.","hi":"गति आय परिवर्तन से तथा स्थानांतरण कीमत परिवर्तन से होता है।"},"3":{"en":"Movement occurs due to own price changes, shift due to other determinants.","hi":"गति स्वयं की कीमत परिवर्तन से तथा स्थानांतरण अन्य निर्धारकों से होता है।"},"4":{"en":"A shift means only a change in quantity demanded.","hi":"स्थानांतरण का अर्थ केवल माँगी गई मात्रा में परिवर्तन है।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Movement occurs due to own price changes, shift due to other determinants.</b><br>A <b>movement along the demand curve</b> (expansion or contraction of demand) occurs because of a change in the <b>own price of the good</b>. A <b>shift of the demand curve</b> (increase or decrease in demand) occurs because of changes in <b>other determinants</b> — income, prices of related goods, tastes, population and expectations.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The demand curve slopes downward because of the <b>law of demand</b>: other things being equal, quantity demanded falls as price rises.<br>• An outward (rightward) shift is an increase in demand, and an inward (leftward) shift is a decrease in demand at the same price.<br>• For normal goods, demand rises with income; for inferior goods, it falls; substitutes and complements affect demand through the prices of related goods.<br>• The same distinction applies to <b>supply curves</b> — movement along the curve is due to own price, and a shift is due to other factors such as technology and input costs.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – गति स्वयं की कीमत परिवर्तन से तथा स्थानांतरण अन्य निर्धारकों से होता है।</b><br><b>माँग वक्र के अनुदिश गति</b> (माँग का विस्तार या संकुचन) वस्तु की <b>स्वयं की कीमत</b> में परिवर्तन से होती है। <b>माँग वक्र का स्थानांतरण</b> (माँग में वृद्धि या कमी) <b>अन्य निर्धारकों</b> — आय, संबंधित वस्तुओं की कीमतें, रुचि, जनसंख्या व प्रत्याशाएँ — में परिवर्तन से होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• माँग वक्र नीचे की ओर ढलवाँ होता है, क्योंकि <b>माँग का नियम</b> कहता है कि अन्य बातें समान रहने पर कीमत बढ़ने से माँगी गई मात्रा घटती है।<br>• बाहर (दाईं ओर) स्थानांतरण माँग में वृद्धि तथा अंदर (बाईं ओर) स्थानांतरण समान कीमत पर माँग में कमी है।<br>• सामान्य वस्तुओं में आय बढ़ने से माँग बढ़ती है; घटिया वस्तुओं में घटती है; स्थानापन्न व पूरक वस्तुएँ संबंधित कीमतों से माँग प्रभावित करती हैं।<br>• यही भेद <b>पूर्ति वक्र</b> पर भी लागू होता है — वक्र के अनुदिश गति स्वयं की कीमत से तथा स्थानांतरण तकनीक व निवेश लागत जैसे कारकों से।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000071027","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Advent of Europeans","question":{"en":"Which technological advantage did the firearms used by the English forces generally have over many traditional weapons used by Indian armies? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"अंग्रेज़ सेनाओं द्वारा प्रयुक्त बंदूकों में भारतीय सेनाओं के अनेक पारंपरिक शस्त्रों की तुलना में सामान्यतः कौन-सा तकनीकी लाभ था? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"They had a shorter range and could be fired less rapidly.","hi":"उनकी परास कम थी और वे कम तेज़ी से दागी जा सकती थीं।"},"2":{"en":"They had a longer range and could be fired more rapidly.","hi":"उनकी परास अधिक थी और वे अधिक तेज़ी से दागी जा सकती थीं।"},"3":{"en":"They were produced locally and could be supplied more easily.","hi":"वे स्थानीय रूप से बनती थीं और आसानी से आपूर्ति हो सकती थीं।"},"4":{"en":"They required less training and could be operated more easily.","hi":"उनके लिए कम प्रशिक्षण चाहिए था और वे आसानी से चलाई जा सकती थीं।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – They had a longer range and could be fired more rapidly.</b><br>The firearms used by English forces — improved <b>matchlock and flintlock muskets and field artillery</b> — generally had a <b>longer range and a faster rate of fire</b> than many traditional Indian weapons such as swords, spears, bows and matchlocks of local make, giving them an advantage in battles such as Plassey and Buxar.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The English introduced <b>standardised muskets and field guns</b> with better gunpowder, drill and disciplined volley fire, along with a well-organised ordinance and supply system.<br>• Indian rulers such as <b>Tipu Sultan</b> and the Marathas also developed artillery and even <b>rocket technology</b> (Tipu’s iron-cased rockets at Srirangapatna).<br>• Superior naval power, discipline and financial resources, rather than firearms alone, explain the eventual English success in India.<br>• The <b>Battle of Plassey (1757)</b> and the <b>Battle of Buxar (1764)</b> established English military supremacy in Bengal.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – उनकी परास अधिक थी और वे अधिक तेज़ी से दागी जा सकती थीं।</b><br>अंग्रेज़ सेनाओं द्वारा प्रयुक्त बंदूकें — उन्नत <b>मैचलॉक व फ्लिंटलॉक मस्केट तथा क्षेत्रीय तोपखाना</b> — की <b>परास लंबी तथा दागने की गति तेज़</b> थी, तलवार, भाला, धनुष तथा स्थानीय निर्मित मैचलॉक जैसे अनेक पारंपरिक भारतीय शस्त्रों की तुलना में, जिससे प्लासी व बक्सर जैसे युद्धों में उन्हें लाभ मिला।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अंग्रेजों ने बेहतर बारूद, ड्रिल व अनुशासित सामूहिक फायर के साथ <b>मानकीकृत मस्केट व तोपें</b> तथा सुनियोजित आयुध-आपूर्ति प्रणाली अपनाई।<br>• <b>टीपू सुल्तान</b> व मराठों ने भी तोपखाना तथा यहाँ तक कि <b>रॉकेट तकनीक</b> (श्रीरंगपटना में टीपू के लोहे के आवरण वाले रॉकेट) विकसित की।<br>• भारत में अंग्रेजों की अंतिम सफलता में केवल बंदूकें नहीं, बल्कि <b>श्रेष्ठ नौसेना शक्ति, अनुशासन व वित्तीय संसाधन</b> कारण थे।<br>• <b>प्लासी (1757)</b> तथा <b>बक्सर (1764)</b> के युद्धों ने बंगाल में अंग्रेज़ सैन्य सर्वोच्चता स्थापित की।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000071028","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: The Mughal Empire","question":{"en":"Which province is described as the richest province of the Mughal Empire? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"मुगल साम्राज्य का सर्वाधिक समृद्ध प्रांत किसे कहा जाता है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Awadh","hi":"अवध"},"2":{"en":"Bengal","hi":"बंगाल"},"3":{"en":"Gujarat","hi":"गुजरात"},"4":{"en":"Malwa","hi":"मालवा"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Bengal</b><br><b>Bengal</b> is described as the <b>richest province of the Mughal Empire</b>. Its fertile delta produced rice, silk and textiles, and its trade through the ports of Hooghly and Chittagong brought large revenue, so that Bengal was called the \"paradise of nations\".<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Bengal’s revenue was the largest among the Mughal subahs, and its <b>muslin and silk</b> were exported to Europe and South-East Asia.<br>• The Mughal subah of Bengal was consolidated by <b>Islam Khan</b> after the defeat of the Afghan and Baro-Bhuyan chiefs; Dhaka became its capital in 1610.<br>• Other prosperous provinces were Gujarat (trade and textiles), Awadh (agriculture and administration) and Malwa (agriculture and trade routes).<br>• The wealth of Bengal later attracted the English East India Company, and after the <b>Battle of Plassey (1757)</b> and Buxar (1764) its revenues passed to the Company.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – बंगाल</b><br><b>बंगाल</b> को <b>मुगल साम्राज्य का सर्वाधिक समृद्ध प्रांत</b> कहा जाता है। उसके उपजाऊ डेल्टा में चावल, रेशम व वस्त्र उत्पन्न होते थे, तथा हुगली व चटगाँव के बंदरगाहों से व्यापार से भारी राजस्व मिलता था, इसीलिए बंगाल को \"राष्ट्रों का स्वर्ग\" कहा गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• बंगाल का राजस्व मुगल सूबों में सर्वाधिक था और वहाँ का <b>मलमल व रेशम</b> यूरोप व दक्षिण-पूर्व एशिया को निर्यात होता था।<br>• बंगाल सूबे को अफगान व बारो-भूयान सरदारों को पराजित करने के बाद <b>इस्लाम खान</b> ने संगठित किया; 1610 में ढाका इसकी राजधानी बनी।<br>• अन्य समृद्ध प्रांत गुजरात (व्यापार व वस्त्र), अवध (कृषि व प्रशासन) तथा मालवा (कृषि व व्यापार मार्ग) थे।<br>• बंगाल की संपदा ने बाद में ईस्ट इंडिया कंपनी को आकर्षित किया, और <b>प्लासी (1757)</b> व बक्सर (1764) के बाद उसका राजस्व कंपनी को मिल गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000071029","section":"GK","topic":"Biology: Heredity and Evolution","question":{"en":"Which type of plasmid lacks a complete conjugation system and therefore requires a self-transmissible helper plasmid for transfer between bacterial cells? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"किस प्रकार के प्लाज्मिड में पूर्ण संयुग्मन प्रणाली नहीं होती और इसलिए जीवाणु कोशिकाओं के बीच स्थानांतरण हेतु स्व-संचरणीय सहायक प्लाज्मिड आवश्यक होता है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Conjugative plasmid","hi":"संयुग्मी प्लाज्मिड"},"2":{"en":"Self-transmissible plasmid","hi":"स्व-संचरणीय प्लाज्मिड"},"3":{"en":"Mobilizable plasmid","hi":"गतिशीलनीय प्लाज्मिड"},"4":{"en":"Col plasmid","hi":"कोल प्लाज्मिड"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Mobilizable plasmid</b><br>A <b>mobilizable (non-conjugative) plasmid</b> carries the <b>oriT</b> sequence and the relaxase gene needed for DNA transfer but lacks the genes for a complete mating-pair formation system. It can therefore be transferred only when a <b>self-transmissible helper plasmid</b> supplies the transfer functions.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Conjugative or self-transmissible plasmids</b> (such as the F plasmid of <i>E. coli</i>) carry the <b>tra</b> genes for sex pilus formation and conjugative transfer.<br>• <b>Col plasmids</b> carry genes for bacteriocins (colicins) that kill related bacteria and may be conjugative or non-conjugative.<br>• Conjugation is the transfer of DNA between bacteria through direct contact, and it is the main route for the spread of <b>antimicrobial resistance genes</b>.<br>• Plasmids are extrachromosomal, circular double-stranded DNA molecules that replicate independently and are widely used as <b>vectors in genetic engineering</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – गतिशीलनीय प्लाज्मिड</b><br><b>गतिशीलनीय (असंयुग्मी) प्लाज्मिड</b> में डीएनए स्थानांतरण हेतु आवश्यक <b>oriT</b> अनुक्रम व रिलैक्सेज जीन होता है, परंतु पूर्ण युग्मन-जोड़ी निर्माण प्रणाली के जीन नहीं होते। अतः यह केवल तब स्थानांतरित हो सकता है जब कोई <b>स्व-संचरणीय सहायक प्लाज्मिड</b> स्थानांतरण कार्य प्रदान करे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>संयुग्मी या स्व-संचरणीय प्लाज्मिड</b> (जैसे ई. कोलाई का F प्लाज्मिड) में लिंग पाइलस बनाने व संयुग्मन स्थानांतरण हेतु <b>tra</b> जीन होते हैं।<br>• <b>कोल प्लाज्मिड</b> बैक्टीरियोसिन (कोलिसिन) हेतु जीन रखते हैं, जो संबंधित जीवाणुओं को मारते हैं, और संयुग्मी या असंयुग्मी हो सकते हैं।<br>• संयुग्मन जीवाणुओं के बीच सीधे संपर्क से डीएनए स्थानांतरण है और <b>प्रतिजैविक प्रतिरोध जीन</b> के प्रसार का मुख्य मार्ग है।<br>• प्लाज्मिड गुणसूत्रेतर, वलयाकार द्विधारी डीएनए अणु हैं जो स्वतंत्र रूप से प्रतिकृत होते हैं और <b>आनुवंशिक अभियांत्रिकी में वेक्टर</b> के रूप में प्रयुक्त होते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000071030","section":"GK","topic":"Biology: Diseases","question":{"en":"Which component of innate immunity functions through a regulated proteolytic cascade that can culminate in membrane attack complex formation and pathogen lysis? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"सहज प्रतिरक्षा का कौन-सा घटक एक नियंत्रित प्रोटियोलिटिक कैस्केड के माध्यम से कार्य करता है, जो झिल्ली आक्रमण परिसंकुल (MAC) बनाकर रोगजनक का लसीकरण (lysis) कर सकता है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Cytokines","hi":"साइटोकाइन"},"2":{"en":"Complement proteins","hi":"पूरक प्रोटीन"},"3":{"en":"Chemokines","hi":"केमोकाइन"},"4":{"en":"Lysozyme","hi":"लाइसोज़ाइम"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Complement proteins</b><br>The <b>complement system</b> is a group of plasma proteins that act through a <b>regulated proteolytic cascade</b> — classical, alternative or lectin pathway — culminating in the formation of the <b>membrane attack complex (MAC)</b>, which creates pores in the pathogen membrane and causes its lysis. Complement proteins also promote opsonisation and inflammation.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The complement system has over <b>30 proteins</b>, with C3 as the central component; the MAC is formed by <b>C5b, C6, C7, C8 and C9</b>.<br>• <b>Cytokines</b> are signalling molecules (interleukins, interferons) and <b>chemokines</b> attract leucocytes to the site of infection.<br>• <b>Lysozyme</b> is an enzyme in tears and saliva that breaks the bacterial cell wall, but it does not act through a proteolytic cascade.<br>• Innate immunity is the first line of defence and is not antigen-specific; adaptive immunity, mediated by B and T cells, provides specific and lasting protection.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – पूरक प्रोटीन</b><br><b>पूरक प्रणाली (complement system)</b> प्लाज्मा प्रोटीनों का समूह है, जो <b>नियंत्रित प्रोटियोलिटिक कैस्केड</b> — चिरसम्मत, वैकल्पिक या लेक्टिन मार्ग — से कार्य करती है और अंत में <b>झिल्ली आक्रमण परिसंकुल (MAC)</b> बनाकर रोगजनक की झिल्ली में छिद्र बनाती है तथा उसका लसीकरण करती है। पूरक प्रोटीन ऑप्सोनीकरण व शोथ को भी बढ़ावा देते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पूरक प्रणाली में <b>30 से अधिक प्रोटीन</b> हैं, जिनमें C3 केंद्रीय घटक है; MAC <b>C5b, C6, C7, C8 व C9</b> से बनता है।<br>• <b>साइटोकाइन</b> संकेत अणु (इंटरल्यूकिन, इंटरफेरॉन) हैं तथा <b>केमोकाइन</b> श्वेत रक्त कोशिकाओं को संक्रमण स्थल की ओर आकर्षित करते हैं।<br>• <b>लाइसोज़ाइम</b> आँसू व लार में मिलने वाला एंजाइम है, जो जीवाणु कोशिका भित्ति तोड़ता है, परंतु प्रोटियोलिटिक कैस्केड से कार्य नहीं करता।<br>• सहज प्रतिरक्षा रक्षा की प्रथम पंक्ति है और प्रतिजन-विशिष्ट नहीं होती; अनुकूली प्रतिरक्षा B व T कोशिकाओं द्वारा विशिष्ट व स्थायी सुरक्षा देती है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000071031","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Evaluate \\(196^2\\). [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"\\(196^2\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"38496"},"2":{"en":"38436"},"3":{"en":"36466"},"4":{"en":"38416"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(196^2 = (200 - 4)^2 = 40000 - 1600 + 16\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{38416}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 38416.</b>","hi":"\\(196^2 = (200 - 4)^2 = 40000 - 1600 + 16\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{38416}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 38416 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000071032","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Find the value of \\(\\frac{3.5 \\times 3.5 \\times 3.5 - 2.5 \\times 2.5 \\times 2.5}{12.25 + 8.75 + 6.25}\\). [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"\\(\\frac{3.5 \\times 3.5 \\times 3.5 - 2.5 \\times 2.5 \\times 2.5}{12.25 + 8.75 + 6.25}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0"},"2":{"en":"1"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"2"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"a = 3.5, b = 2.5 → \\(a^2 = 12.25,\\ ab = 8.75,\\ b^2 = 6.25\\)<br>\\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b\\)<br>\\(= 3.5 - 2.5 = \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1.</b>","hi":"a = 3.5, b = 2.5 → \\(a^2 = 12.25,\\ ab = 8.75,\\ b^2 = 6.25\\)<br>\\(\\frac{a^3 - b^3}{a^2 + ab + b^2} = a - b\\)<br>\\(= 3.5 - 2.5 = \\boxed{1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000071033","section":"MATH","topic":"Pipe and Cistern","question":{"en":"Pipe P can fill a pool in 6 hours, but due to a drainage pipe Q, it takes 9 hours to fill the pool. In how many hours can the drainage pipe Q alone empty the full pool? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पाइप P एक पूल को 6 घंटे में भर सकता है, लेकिन निकास पाइप Q के कारण पूल भरने में 9 घंटे लगते हैं। निकास पाइप Q अकेले भरे हुए पूल को कितने घंटों में खाली कर सकता है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12 hours","hi":"12 घंटे"},"2":{"en":"18 hours","hi":"18 घंटे"},"3":{"en":"16 hours","hi":"16 घंटे"},"4":{"en":"24 hours","hi":"24 घंटे"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Pool = LCM(6, 9) = 18 units<br>P = 3/hr, P − Q = 2/hr → Q = 1/hr<br>Q alone = \\(\\frac{18}{1} = \\boxed{18}\\) hours<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 18 hours.</b>","hi":"पूल = LCM(6, 9) = 18 इकाई<br>P = 3/घंटा, P − Q = 2/घंटा → Q = 1/घंटा<br>Q अकेले = \\(\\frac{18}{1} = \\boxed{18}\\) घंटे<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 18 घंटे है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000071034","section":"MATH","topic":"Ratio and Proportion","question":{"en":"What is the mean proportional between \\(12 - 4\\sqrt{2}\\) and \\(3 + \\sqrt{2}\\)? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"\\(12 - 4\\sqrt{2}\\) और \\(3 + \\sqrt{2}\\) का मध्यानुपाती क्या है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{7}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(3\\sqrt{5}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(6\\sqrt{7}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(7\\sqrt{5}\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Mean proportional = \\(\\sqrt{ab}\\)<br>\\((12 - 4\\sqrt{2})(3 + \\sqrt{2}) = 36 + 12\\sqrt{2} - 12\\sqrt{2} - 8 = 28\\)<br>\\(\\sqrt{28} = \\boxed{2\\sqrt{7}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(2\\sqrt{7}\\).</b>","hi":"मध्यानुपाती = \\(\\sqrt{ab}\\)<br>\\((12 - 4\\sqrt{2})(3 + \\sqrt{2}) = 36 + 12\\sqrt{2} - 12\\sqrt{2} - 8 = 28\\)<br>\\(\\sqrt{28} = \\boxed{2\\sqrt{7}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(2\\sqrt{7}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000071035","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"A sum of ₹15,000 is lent in two parts such that the simple interest on the first part at 10% for 5 years is double the simple interest on the second part at 12.5% for 4 years. What is the difference between the two parts? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"₹15,000 की राशि को दो भागों में इस प्रकार उधार दिया जाता है कि पहले भाग पर 10% की दर से 5 वर्षों का साधारण ब्याज, दूसरे भाग पर 12.5% की दर से 4 वर्षों के साधारण ब्याज का दोगुना है। दोनों भागों का अंतर क्या है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹3,000"},"2":{"en":"₹5,000"},"3":{"en":"₹2,500"},"4":{"en":"₹4,000"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"SI on first part = 50% of x; SI on second part = 50% of y<br>\\(0.5x = 2 \\times 0.5y \\Rightarrow x = 2y\\)<br>\\(3y = 15000 \\Rightarrow y = 5000,\\ x = 10000\\)<br>Difference = \\(\\boxed{5000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹5,000.</b>","hi":"पहले भाग पर साधारण ब्याज = x का 50%; दूसरे भाग पर = y का 50%<br>\\(0.5x = 2 \\times 0.5y \\Rightarrow x = 2y\\)<br>\\(3y = 15000 \\Rightarrow y = 5000,\\ x = 10000\\)<br>अंतर = \\(\\boxed{5000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹5,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000071036","section":"MATH","topic":"Coordinate Geometry","question":{"en":"The graph of \\(y = -3x + 4\\) is parallel to which of the following? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"\\(y = -3x + 4\\) का आलेख निम्नलिखित में से किसके समांतर है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(y = 3x + 4\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(y = -3x - 7\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(3y = x + 2\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(y = 3x - 4\\)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Parallel lines have equal slopes. Slope of \\(y = -3x + 4\\) is −3<br>Slopes of options: 3, −3, \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\), 3<br>Parallel line: \\(\\boxed{y = -3x - 7}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(y = -3x - 7\\).</b>","hi":"समांतर रेखाओं की प्रवणता बराबर होती है। \\(y = -3x + 4\\) की प्रवणता −3 है<br>विकल्पों की प्रवणताएँ: 3, −3, \\(\\frac{1}{3}\\), 3<br>समांतर रेखा: \\(\\boxed{y = -3x - 7}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(y = -3x - 7\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000071037","section":"MATH","topic":"Compound Interest (CI)","question":{"en":"₹1,80,000 is invested at 10% compound interest. After the first year's interest is added, 20% of the interest is withdrawn. Find the balance at the end of 2 years. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"₹1,80,000 को 10% चक्रवृद्धि ब्याज पर निवेश किया जाता है। पहले वर्ष का ब्याज जुड़ने के बाद, ब्याज का 20% निकाल लिया जाता है। 2 वर्ष के अंत में शेष राशि ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹2,53,840"},"2":{"en":"₹2,13,840"},"3":{"en":"₹2,73,840"},"4":{"en":"₹2,93,840"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"1st year interest = 18,000 → Amount = 1,98,000<br>Withdrawn = 20% of 18,000 = 3,600 → Balance = 1,94,400<br>2nd year: \\(194400 \\times 1.1 = \\boxed{213840}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹2,13,840.</b>","hi":"पहले वर्ष का ब्याज = 18,000 → मिश्रधन = 1,98,000<br>निकाली गई राशि = 18,000 का 20% = 3,600 → शेष = 1,94,400<br>दूसरा वर्ष: \\(194400 \\times 1.1 = \\boxed{213840}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹2,13,840 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000071038","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A solid cube with a surface area of 1500 cm² is melted to form smaller cubes, each with a surface area of 60 cm². Find the number of smaller cubes. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"1500 cm² पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल वाले एक ठोस घन को पिघलाकर छोटे घन बनाए जाते हैं, जिनमें से प्रत्येक का पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल 60 cm² है। छोटे घनों की संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"110"},"2":{"en":"150"},"3":{"en":"134"},"4":{"en":"125"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"175\" height=\"145\" viewBox=\"0 0 175 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 45H100V120H20ZM20 45L50 20H130L100 45M130 20V95L100 120\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M50 20V95H130M50 95L20 120\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"138\" y=\"72\">a</text></g></svg><br>Ratio of surface areas = \\(\\frac{1500}{60} = 25\\) → ratio of sides = 5<br>Ratio of volumes = \\(5^3\\)<br>Number of small cubes = \\(\\boxed{125}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 125.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"175\" height=\"145\" viewBox=\"0 0 175 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 45H100V120H20ZM20 45L50 20H130L100 45M130 20V95L100 120\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M50 20V95H130M50 95L20 120\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"138\" y=\"72\">a</text></g></svg><br>पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफलों का अनुपात = \\(\\frac{1500}{60} = 25\\) → भुजाओं का अनुपात = 5<br>आयतनों का अनुपात = \\(5^3\\)<br>छोटे घनों की संख्या = \\(\\boxed{125}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 125 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000071039","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"The diagonals of a rhombus are 32 cm and 24 cm. A new rhombus is formed by joining the midpoints of the sides of the original rhombus. What is the area of the new figure? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक समचतुर्भुज के विकर्ण 32 cm और 24 cm हैं। मूल समचतुर्भुज की भुजाओं के मध्य-बिंदुओं को मिलाकर एक नया समचतुर्भुज बनाया जाता है। नई आकृति का क्षेत्रफल क्या है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"192 cm²"},"2":{"en":"384 cm²"},"3":{"en":"96 cm²"},"4":{"en":"144 cm²"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"150\" height=\"110\" viewBox=\"0 0 150 110\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 55L75 15L130 55L75 95Z\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 55H130M75 15V95\"/><path d=\"M75 48h7v7\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"53\" y=\"51\" text-anchor=\"middle\">32</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"77\">24</text></g></svg><br>Area of original rhombus = \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times 32 \\times 24 = 384\\) cm²<br>Figure formed by joining midpoints has half the area<br>New area = \\(\\frac{384}{2} = \\boxed{192}\\) cm²<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 192 cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"150\" height=\"110\" viewBox=\"0 0 150 110\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 55L75 15L130 55L75 95Z\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 55H130M75 15V95\"/><path d=\"M75 48h7v7\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"53\" y=\"51\" text-anchor=\"middle\">32</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"77\">24</text></g></svg><br>मूल समचतुर्भुज का क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\frac{1}{2} \\times 32 \\times 24 = 384\\) cm²<br>मध्य-बिंदुओं को मिलाने से बनी आकृति का क्षेत्रफल आधा होता है<br>नया क्षेत्रफल = \\(\\frac{384}{2} = \\boxed{192}\\) cm²<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 192 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000071040","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"In a triangle ABC, right-angled at B, if \\(\\cot A = 2\\), find the value of \\(\\frac{\\sin A(\\cos C + \\cos A)}{\\cos C(\\sin C - \\sin A)}\\). [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"B पर समकोण वाले एक त्रिभुज ABC में, यदि \\(\\cot A = 2\\) है, तो \\(\\frac{\\sin A(\\cos C + \\cos A)}{\\cos C(\\sin C - \\sin A)}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{3}\\)"},"2":{"en":"−3"},"3":{"en":"\\(-\\frac{1}{3}\\)"},"4":{"en":"3"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"AB = 2, BC = 1, AC = \\(\\sqrt{5}\\)<br>\\(\\sin A = \\cos C = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}},\\ \\cos A = \\sin C = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\)<br>Value = \\(\\frac{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\times \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}} = \\frac{3/5}{1/5} = \\boxed{3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 3.</b>","hi":"AB = 2, BC = 1, AC = \\(\\sqrt{5}\\)<br>\\(\\sin A = \\cos C = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}},\\ \\cos A = \\sin C = \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\)<br>मान = \\(\\frac{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\times \\frac{3}{\\sqrt{5}}}{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}} = \\frac{3/5}{1/5} = \\boxed{3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000071041","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A right prism has a square base. If the side length of the base is increased by 10% and the height of the prism is decreased by 10%, determine the resulting change in the volume of the prism. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक लंब प्रिज्म का आधार वर्गाकार है। यदि आधार की भुजा की लंबाई में 10% की वृद्धि और प्रिज्म की ऊँचाई में 10% की कमी की जाए, तो प्रिज्म के आयतन में परिणामी परिवर्तन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Increases by 9.2%","hi":"9.2% की वृद्धि"},"2":{"en":"Decreases by 9.2%","hi":"9.2% की कमी"},"3":{"en":"Decreases by 8.9%","hi":"8.9% की कमी"},"4":{"en":"Increases by 8.9%","hi":"8.9% की वृद्धि"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"175\" height=\"145\" viewBox=\"0 0 175 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 45H100V120H20ZM20 45L50 20H130L100 45M130 20V95L100 120\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M50 20V95H130M50 95L20 120\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"138\" y=\"72\">h</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"136\" text-anchor=\"middle\">a</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"116\">a</text></g></svg><br>Volume = \\(a^2 h\\)<br>New volume factor = \\(1.1^2 \\times 0.9 = 1.21 \\times 0.9 = 1.089\\)<br>Change = \\(\\boxed{+8.9\\%}\\) (increase)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Increases by 8.9%.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"175\" height=\"145\" viewBox=\"0 0 175 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M20 45H100V120H20ZM20 45L50 20H130L100 45M130 20V95L100 120\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M50 20V95H130M50 95L20 120\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"138\" y=\"72\">h</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"136\" text-anchor=\"middle\">a</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"116\">a</text></g></svg><br>आयतन = \\(a^2 h\\)<br>नए आयतन का गुणक = \\(1.1^2 \\times 0.9 = 1.21 \\times 0.9 = 1.089\\)<br>परिवर्तन = \\(\\boxed{+8.9\\%}\\) (वृद्धि)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 8.9% की वृद्धि है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000071042","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(x = \\sqrt{\\frac{5 + 2\\sqrt{6}}{5 - 2\\sqrt{6}}}\\), then what is the value of \\(x^2 - 10x + 5\\)? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"यदि \\(x = \\sqrt{\\frac{5 + 2\\sqrt{6}}{5 - 2\\sqrt{6}}}\\) है, तो \\(x^2 - 10x + 5\\) का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(x = \\frac{\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}} = (\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2})^2 = 5 + 2\\sqrt{6}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{x} = 5 - 2\\sqrt{6} \\Rightarrow x + \\frac{1}{x} = 10 \\Rightarrow x^2 - 10x + 1 = 0\\)<br>\\(x^2 - 10x + 5 = 0 + 4 = \\boxed{4}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 4.</b>","hi":"\\(x = \\frac{\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3} - \\sqrt{2}} = (\\sqrt{3} + \\sqrt{2})^2 = 5 + 2\\sqrt{6}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{1}{x} = 5 - 2\\sqrt{6} \\Rightarrow x + \\frac{1}{x} = 10 \\Rightarrow x^2 - 10x + 1 = 0\\)<br>\\(x^2 - 10x + 5 = 0 + 4 = \\boxed{4}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 4 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000071043","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Read the following histogram which represents the time in minutes on x-axis and number of employees on y-axis and answer the following question:<br>What percentage of employees spend more than 31 minutes?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q63.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित आयतचित्र को पढ़िए, जो x-अक्ष पर मिनटों में समय और y-अक्ष पर कर्मचारियों की संख्या दर्शाता है, और निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए:<br>कितने प्रतिशत कर्मचारी 31 मिनट से अधिक समय व्यतीत करते हैं?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q63.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15%"},"2":{"en":"20%"},"3":{"en":"10%"},"4":{"en":"22%"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Frequencies: 16, 18, 23, 20, 11, 12, 10 → Total = 110<br>More than 31 minutes (31–40, 40–50) = 12 + 10 = 22<br>\\(\\frac{22}{110} \\times 100 = \\boxed{20\\%}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 20%.</b>","hi":"आवृत्तियाँ: 16, 18, 23, 20, 11, 12, 10 → कुल = 110<br>31 मिनट से अधिक (31–40, 40–50) = 12 + 10 = 22<br>\\(\\frac{22}{110} \\times 100 = \\boxed{20\\%}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 20% है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q63.jpg"]}},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000071044","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A chord AB of a circle subtends an angle of 120° at a point on the circumference. If the length of AB is \\(5\\sqrt{3}\\) cm, find the radius of the circle. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक वृत्त की जीवा AB परिधि पर स्थित एक बिंदु पर 120° का कोण बनाती है। यदि AB की लंबाई \\(5\\sqrt{3}\\) cm है, तो वृत्त की त्रिज्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{3}\\) cm"},"2":{"en":"5 cm"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{3}\\) cm"},"4":{"en":"10 cm"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"165\" height=\"145\" viewBox=\"0 0 165 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"70\" r=\"55\"/><path d=\"M32 98H128\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M80 70V98M80 70L128 98\"/><path d=\"M87 98v-7h-7\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"70\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"75\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"end\">O</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"end\">A</text><text x=\"132\" y=\"110\">B</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"middle\">M</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"end\">d</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"84\">r</text></g></svg><br>120° at a point on the minor arc → angle on the major arc = 60° → \\(\\angle AOB = 120^\\circ\\)<br>\\(AB = 2r\\sin 60^\\circ = r\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(r\\sqrt{3} = 5\\sqrt{3} \\Rightarrow r = \\boxed{5}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 5 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"165\" height=\"145\" viewBox=\"0 0 165 145\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"70\" r=\"55\"/><path d=\"M32 98H128\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M80 70V98M80 70L128 98\"/><path d=\"M87 98v-7h-7\"/><circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"70\" r=\"1.5\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"75\" y=\"65\" text-anchor=\"end\">O</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"end\">A</text><text x=\"132\" y=\"110\">B</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"112\" text-anchor=\"middle\">M</text><text x=\"75\" y=\"88\" text-anchor=\"end\">d</text><text x=\"110\" y=\"84\">r</text></g></svg><br>लघु चाप पर बिंदु पर 120° → दीर्घ चाप पर कोण = 60° → \\(\\angle AOB = 120^\\circ\\)<br>\\(AB = 2r\\sin 60^\\circ = r\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(r\\sqrt{3} = 5\\sqrt{3} \\Rightarrow r = \\boxed{5}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 5 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000071045","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"Read the following frequency polygon which represents class interval (marks) on the x-axis and frequency (number of students) on the y-axis, and answer the following question:<br>If the pass mark is fixed at 50, how many students failed the exam?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q65.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"निम्नलिखित आवृत्ति बहुभुज को पढ़िए, जो x-अक्ष पर वर्ग अंतराल (अंक) और y-अक्ष पर आवृत्ति (छात्रों की संख्या) दर्शाता है, और निम्नलिखित प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए:<br>यदि उत्तीर्णांक 50 निर्धारित है, तो कितने छात्र परीक्षा में अनुत्तीर्ण हुए?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q65.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"5"},"3":{"en":"12"},"4":{"en":"20"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Frequencies: 30–40: 0, 40–50: 5, 50–60: 12, …<br>Failed = students below 50 = 0 + 5<br>\\(= \\boxed{5}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 5.</b>","hi":"आवृत्तियाँ: 30–40: 0, 40–50: 5, 50–60: 12, …<br>अनुत्तीर्ण = 50 से कम अंक वाले = 0 + 5<br>\\(= \\boxed{5}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q65.jpg"]}},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000071046","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two congruent circles of radius 10 cm intersect in such a way that each passes through the centre of the other. Determine the length of their common chord. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"10 cm त्रिज्या वाले दो सर्वांगसम वृत्त इस प्रकार प्रतिच्छेद करते हैं कि प्रत्येक दूसरे के केंद्र से होकर गुजरता है। उनकी उभयनिष्ठ जीवा की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5 cm"},"2":{"en":"\\(5\\sqrt{3}\\) cm"},"3":{"en":"10 cm"},"4":{"en":"\\(10\\sqrt{3}\\) cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"190\" height=\"150\" viewBox=\"0 0 190 150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"75\" r=\"50\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"75\" r=\"50\"/><path d=\"M95 32V118\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M70 75H120M70 75L95 32\"/><g fill=\"#000\"><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"75\" r=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"75\" r=\"1.5\"/></g><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"66\" y=\"89\" text-anchor=\"end\">O₁</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"89\">O₂</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"27\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"53\" text-anchor=\"end\">10</text><text x=\"107\" y=\"71\">M</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"89\" text-anchor=\"end\">10</text></g></svg><br>Distance between centres = 10 cm → O₁M = 5 cm<br>AM = \\(\\sqrt{10^2 - 5^2} = 5\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>AB = \\(2 \\times 5\\sqrt{3} = \\boxed{10\\sqrt{3}}\\) cm<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(10\\sqrt{3}\\) cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"190\" height=\"150\" viewBox=\"0 0 190 150\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"75\" r=\"50\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"75\" r=\"50\"/><path d=\"M95 32V118\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M70 75H120M70 75L95 32\"/><g fill=\"#000\"><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"75\" r=\"1.5\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"75\" r=\"1.5\"/></g><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"66\" y=\"89\" text-anchor=\"end\">O₁</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"89\">O₂</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"27\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"95\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"middle\">B</text><text x=\"76\" y=\"53\" text-anchor=\"end\">10</text><text x=\"107\" y=\"71\">M</text><text x=\"90\" y=\"89\" text-anchor=\"end\">10</text></g></svg><br>केंद्रों के बीच की दूरी = 10 cm → O₁M = 5 cm<br>AM = \\(\\sqrt{10^2 - 5^2} = 5\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>AB = \\(2 \\times 5\\sqrt{3} = \\boxed{10\\sqrt{3}}\\) cm<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(10\\sqrt{3}\\) cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000071047","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"The ratio of milk and water in a vessel is 8:5. If we add 44 liters of milk and 44 liters of water, then the quantity of milk becomes 28.56% more than the quantity of water. Find the initial quantity of water? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक बर्तन में दूध और पानी का अनुपात 8:5 है। यदि हम 44 लीटर दूध और 44 लीटर पानी मिलाएँ, तो दूध की मात्रा पानी की मात्रा से 28.56% अधिक हो जाती है। पानी की प्रारंभिक मात्रा ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"40 liters","hi":"40 लीटर"},"2":{"en":"45 liters","hi":"45 लीटर"},"3":{"en":"48 liters","hi":"48 लीटर"},"4":{"en":"50 liters","hi":"50 लीटर"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"28.56% ≈ \\(\\frac{2}{7}\\) → new Milk : Water = 9 : 7<br>\\(\\frac{8x + 44}{5x + 44} = \\frac{9}{7} \\Rightarrow 56x + 308 = 45x + 396\\)<br>\\(11x = 88 \\Rightarrow x = 8\\)<br>Initial water = \\(5 \\times 8 = \\boxed{40}\\) L<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 40 liters.</b>","hi":"28.56% ≈ \\(\\frac{2}{7}\\) → नया दूध : पानी = 9 : 7<br>\\(\\frac{8x + 44}{5x + 44} = \\frac{9}{7} \\Rightarrow 56x + 308 = 45x + 396\\)<br>\\(11x = 88 \\Rightarrow x = 8\\)<br>प्रारंभिक पानी = \\(5 \\times 8 = \\boxed{40}\\) L<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 40 लीटर है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000071048","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"Two right circular cylinders have equal volumes. If the ratio of their radii is 7: 9, find the ratio of their heights. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"दो लंब वृत्तीय बेलनों के आयतन बराबर हैं। यदि उनकी त्रिज्याओं का अनुपात 7: 9 है, तो उनकी ऊँचाइयों का अनुपात ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"21:29"},"2":{"en":"29:21"},"3":{"en":"49:81"},"4":{"en":"81:49"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"170\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"12\"/><path d=\"M20 22V112M120 22V112M20 112a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 112a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 22H120M70 22V112\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"31\">7k</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"72\">h₁</text></g></svg>&nbsp; <svg width=\"170\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"12\"/><path d=\"M20 22V112M120 22V112M20 112a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 112a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 22H120M70 22V112\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"31\">9k</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"72\">h₂</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\pi (7k)^2 h_1 = \\pi (9k)^2 h_2\\)<br>\\(\\frac{h_1}{h_2} = \\frac{81}{49}\\)<br>\\(h_1 : h_2 = \\boxed{81 : 49}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 81:49.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"170\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"12\"/><path d=\"M20 22V112M120 22V112M20 112a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 112a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 22H120M70 22V112\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"31\">7k</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"72\">h₁</text></g></svg>&nbsp; <svg width=\"170\" height=\"140\" viewBox=\"0 0 170 140\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><ellipse cx=\"70\" cy=\"22\" rx=\"50\" ry=\"12\"/><path d=\"M20 22V112M120 22V112M20 112a50 12 0 0 0 100 0\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M20 112a50 12 0 0 1 100 0M70 22H120M70 22V112\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"84\" y=\"31\">9k</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"72\">h₂</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\pi (7k)^2 h_1 = \\pi (9k)^2 h_2\\)<br>\\(\\frac{h_1}{h_2} = \\frac{81}{49}\\)<br>\\(h_1 : h_2 = \\boxed{81 : 49}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 81:49 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000071049","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In triangle ABC, a line DE is drawn parallel to side BC. The lengths are given as AD = a, DB = a + 4, AE = 2a + 3, and EC = 7a. Find the value of a, given that a is greater than zero. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"त्रिभुज ABC में, भुजा BC के समांतर एक रेखा DE खींची जाती है। लंबाइयाँ AD = a, DB = a + 4, AE = 2a + 3 और EC = 7a दी गई हैं। a का मान ज्ञात कीजिए, जबकि a शून्य से अधिक है। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"6"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"290\" height=\"170\" viewBox=\"0 0 290 170\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M120 18L40 150H210ZM94 62L150 62\"/><path d=\"M119 58l5 4-5 4M122 146l5 4-5 4\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"120\" y=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"154\">B</text><text x=\"214\" y=\"154\">C</text><text x=\"82\" y=\"66\">D</text><text x=\"155\" y=\"66\">E</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"44\" text-anchor=\"end\">a</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"end\">a + 4</text><text x=\"142\" y=\"44\">2a + 3</text><text x=\"187\" y=\"110\">7a</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{AD}{DB} = \\frac{AE}{EC} \\Rightarrow \\frac{a}{a + 4} = \\frac{2a + 3}{7a}\\)<br>\\(7a^2 = 2a^2 + 11a + 12 \\Rightarrow 5a^2 - 11a - 12 = 0\\)<br>\\((a - 3)(5a + 4) = 0 \\Rightarrow a = \\boxed{3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 3.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"290\" height=\"170\" viewBox=\"0 0 290 170\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M120 18L40 150H210ZM94 62L150 62\"/><path d=\"M119 58l5 4-5 4M122 146l5 4-5 4\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"120\" y=\"13\" text-anchor=\"middle\">A</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"154\">B</text><text x=\"214\" y=\"154\">C</text><text x=\"82\" y=\"66\">D</text><text x=\"155\" y=\"66\">E</text><text x=\"100\" y=\"44\" text-anchor=\"end\">a</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"110\" text-anchor=\"end\">a + 4</text><text x=\"142\" y=\"44\">2a + 3</text><text x=\"187\" y=\"110\">7a</text></g></svg><br>\\(\\frac{AD}{DB} = \\frac{AE}{EC} \\Rightarrow \\frac{a}{a + 4} = \\frac{2a + 3}{7a}\\)<br>\\(7a^2 = 2a^2 + 11a + 12 \\Rightarrow 5a^2 - 11a - 12 = 0\\)<br>\\((a - 3)(5a + 4) = 0 \\Rightarrow a = \\boxed{3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000071050","section":"MATH","topic":"Discount","question":{"en":"A shopkeeper gives a 25% discount on the marked price of a product and still makes a 20% profit, amounting to ₹80. Find the marked price of the product. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक दुकानदार किसी उत्पाद के अंकित मूल्य पर 25% छूट देता है और फिर भी 20% लाभ कमाता है, जो ₹80 के बराबर है। उत्पाद का अंकित मूल्य ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹490"},"2":{"en":"₹720"},"3":{"en":"₹530"},"4":{"en":"₹640"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"20% of CP = 80 → CP = 400, SP = 480<br>SP = 75% of MP<br>MP = \\(\\frac{480}{75} \\times 100 = \\boxed{640}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ₹640.</b>","hi":"क्रय मूल्य का 20% = 80 → क्रय मूल्य = 400, विक्रय मूल्य = 480<br>विक्रय मूल्य = अंकित मूल्य का 75%<br>अंकित मूल्य = \\(\\frac{480}{75} \\times 100 = \\boxed{640}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ₹640 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000071051","section":"MATH","topic":"Data Interpretation (DI)","question":{"en":"The pie chart shows the percentage distribution of literate individuals across different age groups in a survey sample. Study the following pie chart carefully and answer the question given below it.<br>If the total literate population represented in the pie chart is 120,000, what is the average number of literate individuals per age group across the three oldest categories (36–45 years, 46–55 years, and 55+ years)?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q71.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"पाई चार्ट एक सर्वेक्षण नमूने में विभिन्न आयु वर्गों में साक्षर व्यक्तियों का प्रतिशत वितरण दर्शाता है। निम्नलिखित पाई चार्ट का ध्यानपूर्वक अध्ययन कीजिए और नीचे दिए गए प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए।<br>यदि पाई चार्ट में दर्शाई गई कुल साक्षर जनसंख्या 120,000 है, तो तीन सबसे बड़े आयु वर्गों (36–45 वर्ष, 46–55 वर्ष और 55+ वर्ष) में प्रति आयु वर्ग साक्षर व्यक्तियों की औसत संख्या क्या है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q71.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"13,000"},"2":{"en":"16,000"},"3":{"en":"12,000"},"4":{"en":"14,000"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"From the chart: 36–45 = 15%, 46–55 = 10%, 55+ = 5% → total 30%<br>30% of 120000 = 36000<br>Average = \\(\\frac{36000}{3} = \\boxed{12000}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 12,000.</b>","hi":"चार्ट से: 36–45 = 15%, 46–55 = 10%, 55+ = 5% → कुल 30%<br>120000 का 30% = 36000<br>औसत = \\(\\frac{36000}{3} = \\boxed{12000}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 12,000 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q71.jpg"]}},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000071052","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"Two poles of equal height stand on either side of a road 80 m wide. From a point on the road between the poles, the angles of elevation are 60° and 30°. What is the height of each pole? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"80 m चौड़ी सड़क के दोनों ओर समान ऊँचाई के दो खंभे खड़े हैं। खंभों के बीच सड़क पर स्थित एक बिंदु से उन्नयन कोण 60° और 30° हैं। प्रत्येक खंभे की ऊँचाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(20\\sqrt{3}\\) m"},"2":{"en":"\\(40\\sqrt{2}\\) m"},"3":{"en":"\\(25\\sqrt{7}\\) m"},"4":{"en":"\\(35\\sqrt{7}\\) m"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"260\" height=\"142\" viewBox=\"0 0 260 142\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M30 20V107H230V20M30 20L80 107L230 20\"/><path d=\"M64 107A16 16 0 0 1 72 93\"/><path d=\"M96 107A16 16 0 0 0 94 99\"/><path stroke-width=\"1\" d=\"M30 126H230\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"25\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"end\">A</text><text x=\"25\" y=\"111\" text-anchor=\"end\">B</text><text x=\"235\" y=\"24\">C</text><text x=\"235\" y=\"111\">D</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"121\" text-anchor=\"middle\">P</text><text x=\"25\" y=\"67\" text-anchor=\"end\">h</text><text x=\"235\" y=\"67\">h</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"102\" text-anchor=\"end\">60°</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"102\">30°</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"137\" text-anchor=\"middle\">80 m</text></g></svg><br>BP = \\(\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{3}}\\), PD = \\(h\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{3}} + h\\sqrt{3} = 80 \\Rightarrow \\frac{4h}{\\sqrt{3}} = 80\\)<br>\\(h = \\boxed{20\\sqrt{3}}\\) m<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(20\\sqrt{3}\\) m.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"260\" height=\"142\" viewBox=\"0 0 260 142\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M30 20V107H230V20M30 20L80 107L230 20\"/><path d=\"M64 107A16 16 0 0 1 72 93\"/><path d=\"M96 107A16 16 0 0 0 94 99\"/><path stroke-width=\"1\" d=\"M30 126H230\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\"><text x=\"25\" y=\"24\" text-anchor=\"end\">A</text><text x=\"25\" y=\"111\" text-anchor=\"end\">B</text><text x=\"235\" y=\"24\">C</text><text x=\"235\" y=\"111\">D</text><text x=\"80\" y=\"121\" text-anchor=\"middle\">P</text><text x=\"25\" y=\"67\" text-anchor=\"end\">h</text><text x=\"235\" y=\"67\">h</text><text x=\"58\" y=\"102\" text-anchor=\"end\">60°</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"102\">30°</text><text x=\"130\" y=\"137\" text-anchor=\"middle\">80 m</text></g></svg><br>BP = \\(\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{3}}\\), PD = \\(h\\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(\\frac{h}{\\sqrt{3}} + h\\sqrt{3} = 80 \\Rightarrow \\frac{4h}{\\sqrt{3}} = 80\\)<br>\\(h = \\boxed{20\\sqrt{3}}\\) m<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(20\\sqrt{3}\\) m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000071053","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"A square garden has side \\((6x + 5y)\\) meters. A square pond inside it has side \\((2x + y)\\) meters. Find the area of the garden excluding the pond in square meters, where \\(x, y \\gt 0\\). [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक वर्गाकार बगीचे की भुजा \\((6x + 5y)\\) मीटर है। इसके अंदर एक वर्गाकार तालाब की भुजा \\((2x + y)\\) मीटर है। तालाब को छोड़कर बगीचे का क्षेत्रफल वर्ग मीटर में ज्ञात कीजिए, जहाँ \\(x, y \\gt 0\\)। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(8(x + y)(4x + 3y)\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(8(2x + y)(4x + 3y)\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(8(x + 2y)(5x + 3y)\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(2(x + y)(4x + 5y)\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Area = \\((6x + 5y)^2 - (2x + y)^2\\)<br>\\(= (6x + 5y + 2x + y)(6x + 5y - 2x - y) = (8x + 6y)(4x + 4y)\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{8(x + y)(4x + 3y)}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(8(x + y)(4x + 3y)\\).</b>","hi":"क्षेत्रफल = \\((6x + 5y)^2 - (2x + y)^2\\)<br>\\(= (6x + 5y + 2x + y)(6x + 5y - 2x - y) = (8x + 6y)(4x + 4y)\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{8(x + y)(4x + 3y)}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(8(x + y)(4x + 3y)\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000071054","section":"MATH","topic":"Average","question":{"en":"The average of n consecutive multiples of 11 is 143. If the difference between the largest and the smallest number in the set is 132, find the value of n. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"11 के n क्रमागत गुणजों का औसत 143 है। यदि समुच्चय की सबसे बड़ी और सबसे छोटी संख्या का अंतर 132 है, तो n का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"10"},"2":{"en":"11"},"3":{"en":"12"},"4":{"en":"13"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Consecutive multiples of 11 differ by 11<br>Largest − Smallest = \\(11(n - 1) = 132\\)<br>\\(n - 1 = 12 \\Rightarrow n = \\boxed{13}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 13.</b>","hi":"11 के क्रमागत गुणजों में अंतर 11 होता है<br>सबसे बड़ी − सबसे छोटी = \\(11(n - 1) = 132\\)<br>\\(n - 1 = 12 \\Rightarrow n = \\boxed{13}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 13 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000071055","section":"MATH","topic":"Elementary Statistics","question":{"en":"A psychological research study analyzes the frequency distribution of spatial-coordination errors made by participants using a complex flight simulator layout. The observations are as given in the bar graph below:<br>Identify the error category that has the highest frequency and the error categories that have the lowest non-zero frequency. What is the minimum absolute numerical difference between the numerical value of the highest-frequency category and the numerical value of any of the lowest non-zero frequency categories?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q75.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]","hi":"एक मनोवैज्ञानिक शोध अध्ययन, एक जटिल फ्लाइट सिम्युलेटर लेआउट का उपयोग करने वाले प्रतिभागियों द्वारा की गई स्थानिक-समन्वय त्रुटियों के आवृत्ति वितरण का विश्लेषण करता है। प्रेक्षण नीचे दिए गए दंड आलेख में दिए गए हैं:<br>सबसे अधिक आवृत्ति वाली त्रुटि श्रेणी और सबसे कम शून्येतर आवृत्ति वाली त्रुटि श्रेणियों की पहचान कीजिए। सबसे अधिक आवृत्ति वाली श्रेणी के संख्यात्मक मान और सबसे कम शून्येतर आवृत्ति वाली किसी भी श्रेणी के संख्यात्मक मान के बीच न्यूनतम निरपेक्ष संख्यात्मक अंतर क्या है?<br><img src=\"https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q75.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto\"> [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"2"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Frequencies: errors 0 → 8, 1 → 15, 2 → 22, 3 → 30, 4 → 17, 5 → 8<br>Highest frequency: category 3; lowest non-zero frequency (8): categories 0 and 5<br>Minimum difference = \\(\\min(|3 - 0|, |3 - 5|) = \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 2.</b>","hi":"आवृत्तियाँ: त्रुटि 0 → 8, 1 → 15, 2 → 22, 3 → 30, 4 → 17, 5 → 8<br>सबसे अधिक आवृत्ति: श्रेणी 3; सबसे कम शून्येतर आवृत्ति (8): श्रेणियाँ 0 और 5<br>न्यूनतम अंतर = \\(\\min(|3 - 0|, |3 - 5|) = \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":true,"images":{"question":["https://res.cloudinary.com/mc6kb3uo/image/upload/ssc_mock/CGL-13-OCT-2026-SHIFT-3/q75.jpg"]}}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000071056","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Select the wrongly spelt word out of the four alternatives. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Assassination"},"2":{"en":"Unacustomed"},"3":{"en":"Ruthlessness"},"4":{"en":"Liaison"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Unaccustomed (अनभ्यस्त) = not familiar with or used to something.</b><br><b>Unacustomed</b> omits one “c” and one “s”; the correct form is “unaccustomed.”<br><b>Assassination (हत्या)</b> = murder of a prominent person; spelling correct.<br><b>Ruthlessness (निर्दयता)</b> = cruelty; <b>liaison (सम्पर्क)</b> = communication or connection.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Unacustomed.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000071057","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Select the wrongly spelt word out of the four alternatives. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Brusquely"},"2":{"en":"Messenjer"},"3":{"en":"Absolute"},"4":{"en":"Exhausted"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Messenger (संदेशवाहक) = a person who carries a message.</b><br><b>Messenjer</b> wrongly uses “j” instead of “g.”<br><b>Brusquely (रूखेपन से)</b> = curtly; spelling correct.<br><b>Absolute (पूर्ण)</b> = complete; <b>exhausted (थका हुआ)</b> = extremely tired.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Messenjer.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000071058","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Choose the most appropriate antonym of the underlined word.<br>The prime minister gave a <u>perfunctory</u> nod to the reporters. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Thorough"},"2":{"en":"Hasty"},"3":{"en":"Casual"},"4":{"en":"Careless"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Perfunctory (औपचारिकता मात्र) = done with minimal effort or care.</b><br><b>Thorough (पूर्ण, गहन)</b> = done with great care and completeness ✔<br><b>Hasty (जल्दबाज)</b> = done hurriedly<br><b>Casual (अनौपचारिक)</b> = informal or unconcerned<br><b>Careless (लापरवाह)</b> = lacking attention<br>More antonyms: meticulous, diligent, attentive.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Thorough.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000071059","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Choose the most appropriate antonym of the underlined word.<br>The school enforced <u>stringent</u> rules regarding student attendance. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Lax"},"2":{"en":"Firm"},"3":{"en":"Rigorous"},"4":{"en":"Strict"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Stringent (कठोर) = strict, precise and demanding.</b><br><b>Lax (ढीला)</b> = not sufficiently strict ✔<br><b>Firm (दृढ़)</b> = resolute<br><b>Rigorous (कठोर)</b> = extremely thorough and strict<br><b>Strict (सख्त)</b> = demanding obedience<br>More antonyms: lenient, flexible, permissive.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Lax.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000071060","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Select the correctly spelt word to replace the highlighted word in the given sentence.<br>His <b>averice</b> led to his eventual downfall. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Avarice"},"2":{"en":"Averice"},"3":{"en":"Avwarice"},"4":{"en":"Avarise"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Avarice (लोभ) = extreme greed for wealth.</b><br>The correct spelling is “avarice.”<br><b>Averice</b> replaces “a” with “e” after “v”; <b>Avwarice</b> wrongly inserts “w.”<br><b>Avarise</b> changes the ending to “-ise.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Avarice.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000071061","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Select the correctly spelt word to replace the highlighted word in the given sentence.<br>His <b>punicious</b> habits eventually led to a very serious illness. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Pernicious"},"2":{"en":"Pernicius"},"3":{"en":"Punicious"},"4":{"en":"Pernicous"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Pernicious (घातक) = having a very harmful effect.</b><br>The correct spelling is “pernicious.”<br><b>Pernicius</b> omits “o” before “us”; <b>Punicious</b> omits “er.”<br><b>Pernicous</b> omits “i” before “ous.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Pernicious.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000071062","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"In the following question, the first and last parts of the sentence (1 and 6) are given. The rest of the sentence is split into four parts and named P, Q, R, and S. These four parts are not given in their proper order. Read the sentence and find out which of the four combinations is correct.<br>1. Our ability to<br>P. of others is what<br>Q. and feel the emotions<br>R. understand the perspectives<br>S. makes us truly<br>6. compassionate human beings. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PQSR"},"2":{"en":"RSPQ"},"3":{"en":"RPSQ"},"4":{"en":"RQPS"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: RQPS</b><br>R follows “Our ability to understand the perspectives.”<br>Q adds “and feel the emotions,” and P supplies “of others is what.”<br>S connects this ability to part 6: it makes us truly compassionate human beings.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): RQPS.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000071063","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"In the following question, the first and last parts of the sentence (1 and 6) are given. The rest of the sentence is split into four parts and named P, Q, R, and S. These four parts are not given in their proper order. Read the sentence and find out which of the four combinations is correct.<br>1. It is widely<br>P. to the environment<br>Q. believed that the<br>R. poses a serious threat<br>S. use of plastic bags<br>6. and our marine life. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QSRP"},"2":{"en":"PRSQ"},"3":{"en":"QRPS"},"4":{"en":"QRSP"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QSRP</b><br>Q completes “It is widely believed that the.”<br>S supplies the subject “use of plastic bags,” and R gives the predicate “poses a serious threat.”<br>P joins part 6 to name what is threatened: the environment and marine life.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): QSRP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000071064","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"From the given options, select the homonym that corresponds to both Definition (P) and Definition (Q).<br>(P) A military flag, banner, or symbolic staff raised to mark the rally point of an army<br>(Q) An officially approved level of quality, requirement, or specification [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Benchmark"},"2":{"en":"Insignia"},"3":{"en":"Criteria"},"4":{"en":"Standard"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Standard (ध्वज; मानक)</b><br>A standard can be a military flag or rallying banner.<br>It also means an officially accepted level of quality or requirement.<br>Benchmark is a reference point, insignia is a badge, and criteria are principles of judgement.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Standard.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000071065","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Identify the option in which the underlined idiom has been used incorrectly.<br>A. The elite research institute's academic curriculum is widely considered <u>a cut above</u> that of regional universities, owing to its mandatory advanced robotics modules and global lab partnerships.<br>B. The lead actors met for the first time during the table read and <u>hit it off</u>, resulting in an uncomfortable, visible lack of chemistry on set that forced the director to repeatedly pause production.<br>C. Before initiating the cross-border merger, the lead legal strategist spent several weeks analysing the rival firm's previous litigation history to <u>take the measure of</u> their executive board.<br>D. Trailing by fifteen points in the final quarter, the underdog basketball team completely <u>turned the tables</u> by executing a relentless full-court press and securing a dramatic one-point victory at the buzzer. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The elite research institute's academic curriculum is widely considered a cut above that of regional universities, owing to its mandatory advanced robotics modules and global lab partnerships."},"2":{"en":"The lead actors met for the first time during the table read and hit it off, resulting in an uncomfortable, visible lack of chemistry on set that forced the director to repeatedly pause production."},"3":{"en":"Before initiating the cross-border merger, the lead legal strategist spent several weeks analysing the rival firm's previous litigation history to take the measure of their executive board."},"4":{"en":"Trailing by fifteen points in the final quarter, the underdog basketball team completely turned the tables by executing a relentless full-court press and securing a dramatic one-point victory at the buzzer."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Hit it off (अच्छे संबंध बनाना) = immediately like each other and get along well.</b><br>A visible lack of chemistry contradicts this meaning, so option B uses the idiom incorrectly.<br>“A cut above” correctly means superior; “take the measure of” means assess.<br>“Turned the tables” correctly describes reversing a disadvantage into victory.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The lead actors met for the first time during the table read and hit it off, resulting in an uncomfortable, visible lack of chemistry on set that forced the director to repeatedly pause production.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000071066","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Fill in the blanks with the correct option, ensuring the verb tenses accurately reflect the chronological sequence of events.<br>Scarcely ___ the morning train when I realized that, if I had left my house five minutes later, I ___ the crucial interview. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"I had boarded, missed"},"2":{"en":"had I boarded, would have missed"},"3":{"en":"did I board, would miss"},"4":{"en":"had I boarded, will miss"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Scarcely” triggers inversion; an unreal past condition uses “would have + past participle.”</b><br>“Had I boarded” gives the required inversion after “scarcely.”<br>The missed interview is the unreal past result, so “would have missed” is correct.<br>The other options lack the required inversion or conditional form.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): had I boarded, would have missed.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000071067","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"The sentence below is divided into two parts labelled P and Q. Identify which sentence contains a grammatical or idiomatic error.<br>P: The corporate legal team meticulously ironed out the final merger documents with the target firm's underwriters before the executive board signed them.<br>Q: During the high-pressure restructuring session in the unventilated boardroom, the junior analyst suddenly passed out from heat exhaustion. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only P"},"2":{"en":"Only Q"},"3":{"en":"Both P and Q"},"4":{"en":"Neither P nor Q"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Both sentences use their phrasal verbs correctly.</b><br>“Ironed out” means resolved difficulties or finalized details.<br>“Passed out” means lost consciousness, which fits heat exhaustion.<br>Neither P nor Q contains a grammatical or idiomatic error.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Neither P nor Q.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000071068","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Read the two sentences given below carefully and identify which one contains a grammatical error.<br>P: The target software corporation implemented an aggressive poison-pill strategy to fend off against the hostile takeover bid initiated by the activist hedge fund.<br>Q: During the cross-border corporate fraud investigation, the forensic accounting team began to home in on the anomalous shell company transactions routed through offshore tax havens. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only P"},"2":{"en":"Only Q"},"3":{"en":"Both P and Q"},"4":{"en":"Neither P nor Q"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Fend off” is transitive and does not take “against.”</b><br>P should read “to <b>fend off</b> the hostile takeover bid.”<br>Q correctly uses “home in on,” meaning focus attention on a target.<br>Therefore, only P contains an error.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only P.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000071069","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Three of the options below represent incorrect or ungrammatical attempts to modify the sentence. Select the single alternative that successfully achieves a correct active voice transformation.<br>A gathering is formed by local workers to hear Raghav’s situation recounted, and gentle corrections are made by them regarding the name of the mill worker being sought by him, yet no concern is felt by him over this discrepancy, and absolute confidence is maintained by him that his companion will be located. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Local workers form a gathering to hear Raghav’s situation recounted, and they made gentle corrections regarding the name of the mill worker he is seeking, yet he feels no concern over this discrepancy and maintained absolute confidence that he will locate his companion."},"2":{"en":"Local workers from a gathering to hear Raghav's situation recount, and they make gentle corrections regarding the name of the mill worker he is seeking, yet he feels no concern over this discrepancy and maintains absolute confidence that he will locate his companion."},"3":{"en":"Local workers form a gathering to hear Raghav’s situation recounted, and they make gentle corrections regarding the name of the mill worker he is seeking, yet he feels no concern over this discrepancy and maintains absolute confidence that he will locate his companion."},"4":{"en":"Local workers form a gathering to hear Raghav’s situation recount, and they made gentle corrections regarding the name of the mill worker he is seeking, yet he feels no concern over this discrepancy and maintains absolute confidence that he locate his companion."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: The agents become subjects, and present-tense passive verbs become active.</b><br>“Local workers form” and “they make” correctly replace “is formed” and “are made.”<br>“He feels” and “maintains” replace “is felt” and “is maintained.”<br>A inconsistently shifts to past tense; B uses “from” instead of “form”; D changes tense and omits “will.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Local workers form a gathering to hear Raghav’s situation recounted, and they make gentle corrections regarding the name of the mill worker he is seeking, yet he feels no concern over this discrepancy and maintains absolute confidence that he will locate his companion.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000071070","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Read the following sentence carefully, focusing on the underlined portion. Select the option (A/B/C) that can suitably substitute the underlined segment to improve the given sentence. If the sentence is correct as written, then select Option D (No improvement required).<br>When the museum conservation team carefully applied the newly formulated chemical solvent to the damaged Renaissance fresco, <u>it dissolved almost instantly, causing widespread panic amidst the curators</u>. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"they dissolved almost instantly, a reaction which caused widespread panic around the curators"},"2":{"en":"the solvent dissolved almost instantly, that caused widespread panic in the curators"},"3":{"en":"the fresco dissolved almost instantly, causing widespread panic among the curators"},"4":{"en":"No improvement required"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: A pronoun must clearly identify its intended antecedent.</b><br>The fresco, not the conservation team or solvent, dissolved.<br>“Among the curators” is the idiomatic preposition for panic shared within a group.<br>A and B identify the wrong subjects and use awkward relative constructions; D retains the ambiguity.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): the fresco dissolved almost instantly, causing widespread panic among the curators.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000071071","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Read the following sentence carefully, focusing on the underlined portion. Select the option (A/B/C) that can suitably substitute the underlined segment to improve the given sentence. If the sentence is correct as written, then select Option D (No improvement required).<br>The multinational technology conglomerate officially absorbed the boutique software startup <u>because they possessed a highly lucrative proprietary algorithm that promised to dominate</u> the global market. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"as it possessed a highly lucrative proprietary algorithm who promised to dominate"},"2":{"en":"because the startup possessed a highly lucrative proprietary algorithm that promised to dominate"},"3":{"en":"Since the conglomerate possessed a highly lucrative proprietary algorithm which promised to dominate"},"4":{"en":"No improvement required"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Replace the ambiguous plural pronoun “they” with the intended entity.</b><br>The startup possessed the algorithm, so naming it removes ambiguity.<br>A uses “who” for an algorithm; C incorrectly attributes ownership to the conglomerate.<br>D leaves unclear whether the conglomerate or startup possessed it.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): because the startup possessed a highly lucrative proprietary algorithm that promised to dominate.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000071072","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Convert the following sentence from direct to indirect speech. Choose the option that best represents the correct transformation.<br>Harman said to Lipika, “If you had observed us during our transit between facilities, as we watched the mountain peaks illuminated by the sunset through the small, restricted windows of our transport vehicle, you would never have guessed that we had previously abandoned all expectations of our future.” [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Harman told Lipika that if she had observed them during their transit between facilities, as they had watched the mountain peaks illuminated by the sunset through the small, restricted windows of their transport vehicle, she would never have guessed that they had previously abandoned all expectations of their future."},"2":{"en":"Harman told Lipika that if she observed them during their transit between facilities, as they had watched the mountain peaks illuminated by the sunset through the small, restricted windows of their transport vehicle, she would never have guessed that they had previously abandoned all expectations of their future."},"3":{"en":"Harman told Lipika that if she had observed them during their transit between facilities, as they had watched the mountain peaks illuminated by the sunset through the small, restricted windows of their transport vehicle, she would never guess that they had previously abandoned all expectations of their future."},"4":{"en":"Harman told Lipika that if she had observed them during their transit between facilities, as they had watched the mountain peaks illuminated by the sunset through the small, restricted windows of their transport vehicle, she would never have guessed that they would have previously abandoned all expectations of their future."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Change pronouns to third person and backshift “watched” to “had watched.”</b><br>The unreal-past frame “if she had observed … she would never have guessed” remains intact.<br>B omits the required past perfect in the if-clause; C changes the result.<br>D incorrectly inserts “would have” into the embedded abandonment clause.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Harman told Lipika that if she had observed them during their transit between facilities, as they had watched the mountain peaks illuminated by the sunset through the small, restricted windows of their transport vehicle, she would never have guessed that they had previously abandoned all expectations of their future.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000071073","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Select the option that correctly converts the following indirect statement into direct speech.<br>Swati told Kashvi that she had learned to fly in order to come to terms with her fear of heights, and to think highly of humanity by meeting labourers at their local inn who had led lives of destitution and had worked on towers that had been several feet tall. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Swati said to Kashvi, “I learned to fly in order to come to terms with my fear of heights, and thought highly of humanity by meeting labourers at our local inn who led lives of destitution and worked on towers that were several feet tall.”"},"2":{"en":"Swati said to Kashvi, “I learned to fly in order to come to terms with my fear of heights, and to think highly of humanity by having met labourers at our local inn who led lives of destitution and worked on towers that were several feet tall.”"},"3":{"en":"Swati said to Kashvi, “I learned to fly in order to come to terms with my fear of heights, and to think highly of humanity by meeting labourers at our local inn who led lives of destitution and worked on towers that were several feet tall.”"},"4":{"en":"Swati said to Kashvi, “I learned to fly in order to come to terms with my fear of heights, and to think highly of humanity by meeting labourers at our local inn who lead lives of destitution and worked on towers that were several feet tall.”"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Restore first-person pronouns and simple past forms.</b><br>“Had learned” becomes “learned,” “had led” becomes “led,” and “had been” becomes “were.”<br>A changes “to think” to “thought”; B changes “meeting” to “having met.”<br>D uses present “lead” instead of past “led.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Swati said to Kashvi, “I learned to fly in order to come to terms with my fear of heights, and to think highly of humanity by meeting labourers at our local inn who led lives of destitution and worked on towers that were several feet tall.”.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000071074","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Select the correct passive form of the given sentence.<br>Nobody had informed the passengers about the sudden change in the flight route. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The passengers had not been informed about the sudden change in the flight route."},"2":{"en":"The passengers were not informed about the sudden change in the flight route by nobody."},"3":{"en":"The passengers have not been informed about the sudden change in the flight route."},"4":{"en":"The passengers had not been informed about the sudden change in the flight route by nobody."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Past perfect passive = had been + past participle; “nobody” becomes “not.”</b><br>The passengers become the subject, and no agent needs to be stated.<br>B changes the tense and awkwardly retains “nobody.”<br>C uses present perfect; D redundantly includes “by nobody.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): The passengers had not been informed about the sudden change in the flight route.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000071075","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Choose the option that provides the correct sequence of prepositions to complete the sentence grammatically.<br>The philosopher contended that morality exists ___ the realm of legality, operates ___ opposition to utilitarianism, and persists ___ spite of cultural relativism. [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"within, against, despite"},"2":{"en":"beyond, in, in"},"3":{"en":"beneath, concerning, owing to"},"4":{"en":"alongside, with, prior to"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct phrases: “beyond the realm of,” “in opposition to,” and “in spite of.”</b><br>“Beyond” places morality outside legality; “in opposition to” expresses conflict with utilitarianism.<br>“In spite of” means despite cultural relativism.<br>The other sequences do not produce these standard expressions.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): beyond, in, in.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000071076","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the passage by choosing the most appropriate words for the blanks.<br><br>Responsible tourism has emerged as an essential principle in an era when travel has become more accessible than ever before. While tourism generates employment, strengthens local economies, and encourages cultural exchange, it can also impose significant pressure on fragile ecosystems and traditional communities. (A)___, policymakers, businesses, and travellers must collectively ensure that economic benefits do not come at the expense of environmental sustainability or cultural integrity. Responsible tourism is not merely about reducing waste or avoiding plastic; it also requires visitors to understand the social and historical contexts of the destinations they explore. Such awareness encourages tourists to make (B)___ decisions that support local artisans, conserve natural resources, and respect indigenous customs. If tourism authorities (C)___ stricter sustainability standards and monitored their implementation consistently, many ecological challenges associated with mass tourism could be substantially reduced. Equally important is the need for tourism operators to (D)___ between commercial profitability and ecological responsibility. Long-term prosperity depends not only on attracting more visitors but also on preserving the very landscapes and traditions that make destinations distinctive. Travellers, too, must recognise that every journey carries ethical implications. Choosing locally owned accommodations, minimising resource consumption, and engaging respectfully (E)___ host communities contribute to a tourism model that benefits both present and future generations. Ultimately, responsible tourism is less about restricting movement than about cultivating thoughtful habits that transform travel into a mutually enriching experience for visitors and residents alike.<br><br><br>Identify the correct discourse marker for blank (A). [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Nevertheless"},"2":{"en":"Therefore"},"3":{"en":"Likewise"},"4":{"en":"Meanwhile"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Therefore (इसलिए) introduces a conclusion or required response.</b><br>Tourism’s environmental and cultural pressures lead to the need for collective responsibility.<br>“Nevertheless” expresses contrast; “likewise” expresses similarity.<br>“Meanwhile” marks simultaneous time and does not convey the inference.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Therefore.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000071077","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the passage by choosing the most appropriate words for the blanks.<br><br>Responsible tourism has emerged as an essential principle in an era when travel has become more accessible than ever before. While tourism generates employment, strengthens local economies, and encourages cultural exchange, it can also impose significant pressure on fragile ecosystems and traditional communities. (A)___, policymakers, businesses, and travellers must collectively ensure that economic benefits do not come at the expense of environmental sustainability or cultural integrity. Responsible tourism is not merely about reducing waste or avoiding plastic; it also requires visitors to understand the social and historical contexts of the destinations they explore. Such awareness encourages tourists to make (B)___ decisions that support local artisans, conserve natural resources, and respect indigenous customs. If tourism authorities (C)___ stricter sustainability standards and monitored their implementation consistently, many ecological challenges associated with mass tourism could be substantially reduced. Equally important is the need for tourism operators to (D)___ between commercial profitability and ecological responsibility. Long-term prosperity depends not only on attracting more visitors but also on preserving the very landscapes and traditions that make destinations distinctive. Travellers, too, must recognise that every journey carries ethical implications. Choosing locally owned accommodations, minimising resource consumption, and engaging respectfully (E)___ host communities contribute to a tourism model that benefits both present and future generations. Ultimately, responsible tourism is less about restricting movement than about cultivating thoughtful habits that transform travel into a mutually enriching experience for visitors and residents alike.<br><br><br>Identify the correct word for blank (B). [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"informed"},"2":{"en":"impulsive"},"3":{"en":"arbitrary"},"4":{"en":"reluctant"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Informed (सूचित, जानकारीपूर्ण) = based on knowledge and understanding.</b><br>Awareness of social and historical contexts leads tourists to make informed decisions.<br><b>Impulsive (आवेगी)</b> = acting without thought<br><b>Arbitrary (मनमाना)</b> = random; <b>reluctant (अनिच्छुक)</b> = unwilling<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): informed.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000071078","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the passage by choosing the most appropriate words for the blanks.<br><br>Responsible tourism has emerged as an essential principle in an era when travel has become more accessible than ever before. While tourism generates employment, strengthens local economies, and encourages cultural exchange, it can also impose significant pressure on fragile ecosystems and traditional communities. (A)___, policymakers, businesses, and travellers must collectively ensure that economic benefits do not come at the expense of environmental sustainability or cultural integrity. Responsible tourism is not merely about reducing waste or avoiding plastic; it also requires visitors to understand the social and historical contexts of the destinations they explore. Such awareness encourages tourists to make (B)___ decisions that support local artisans, conserve natural resources, and respect indigenous customs. If tourism authorities (C)___ stricter sustainability standards and monitored their implementation consistently, many ecological challenges associated with mass tourism could be substantially reduced. Equally important is the need for tourism operators to (D)___ between commercial profitability and ecological responsibility. Long-term prosperity depends not only on attracting more visitors but also on preserving the very landscapes and traditions that make destinations distinctive. Travellers, too, must recognise that every journey carries ethical implications. Choosing locally owned accommodations, minimising resource consumption, and engaging respectfully (E)___ host communities contribute to a tourism model that benefits both present and future generations. Ultimately, responsible tourism is less about restricting movement than about cultivating thoughtful habits that transform travel into a mutually enriching experience for visitors and residents alike.<br><br><br>Identify the correct word/phrase for blank (C). [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"enforce"},"2":{"en":"have enforced"},"3":{"en":"had enforced"},"4":{"en":"enforced"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: An unreal present condition uses simple past in the if-clause.</b><br>“If tourism authorities <b>enforced</b> stricter standards and monitored …” parallels “could be reduced.”<br>“Enforce” does not fit the unreal conditional; present perfect and past perfect change the time relationship.<br>The parallel “monitored” also confirms simple past.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): enforced.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000071079","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the passage by choosing the most appropriate words for the blanks.<br><br>Responsible tourism has emerged as an essential principle in an era when travel has become more accessible than ever before. While tourism generates employment, strengthens local economies, and encourages cultural exchange, it can also impose significant pressure on fragile ecosystems and traditional communities. (A)___, policymakers, businesses, and travellers must collectively ensure that economic benefits do not come at the expense of environmental sustainability or cultural integrity. Responsible tourism is not merely about reducing waste or avoiding plastic; it also requires visitors to understand the social and historical contexts of the destinations they explore. Such awareness encourages tourists to make (B)___ decisions that support local artisans, conserve natural resources, and respect indigenous customs. If tourism authorities (C)___ stricter sustainability standards and monitored their implementation consistently, many ecological challenges associated with mass tourism could be substantially reduced. Equally important is the need for tourism operators to (D)___ between commercial profitability and ecological responsibility. Long-term prosperity depends not only on attracting more visitors but also on preserving the very landscapes and traditions that make destinations distinctive. Travellers, too, must recognise that every journey carries ethical implications. Choosing locally owned accommodations, minimising resource consumption, and engaging respectfully (E)___ host communities contribute to a tourism model that benefits both present and future generations. Ultimately, responsible tourism is less about restricting movement than about cultivating thoughtful habits that transform travel into a mutually enriching experience for visitors and residents alike.<br><br><br>Identify the correct phrase for blank (D). [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"draw a balance"},"2":{"en":"strike a balance"},"3":{"en":"build a balance"},"4":{"en":"create a balance"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Collocation: “Strike a balance between X and Y.”</b><br>Tourism operators must balance commercial profitability and ecological responsibility.<br>“Draw,” “build” and “create” are not standard verbs in this idiom.<br>The established phrase is “strike a balance.”<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): strike a balance.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000071080","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Cloze Test","question":{"en":"Complete the passage by choosing the most appropriate words for the blanks.<br><br>Responsible tourism has emerged as an essential principle in an era when travel has become more accessible than ever before. While tourism generates employment, strengthens local economies, and encourages cultural exchange, it can also impose significant pressure on fragile ecosystems and traditional communities. (A)___, policymakers, businesses, and travellers must collectively ensure that economic benefits do not come at the expense of environmental sustainability or cultural integrity. Responsible tourism is not merely about reducing waste or avoiding plastic; it also requires visitors to understand the social and historical contexts of the destinations they explore. Such awareness encourages tourists to make (B)___ decisions that support local artisans, conserve natural resources, and respect indigenous customs. If tourism authorities (C)___ stricter sustainability standards and monitored their implementation consistently, many ecological challenges associated with mass tourism could be substantially reduced. Equally important is the need for tourism operators to (D)___ between commercial profitability and ecological responsibility. Long-term prosperity depends not only on attracting more visitors but also on preserving the very landscapes and traditions that make destinations distinctive. Travellers, too, must recognise that every journey carries ethical implications. Choosing locally owned accommodations, minimising resource consumption, and engaging respectfully (E)___ host communities contribute to a tourism model that benefits both present and future generations. Ultimately, responsible tourism is less about restricting movement than about cultivating thoughtful habits that transform travel into a mutually enriching experience for visitors and residents alike.<br><br><br>Identify the correct word for blank (E). [SSC CGL 13/10/26 Shift 3]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"to"},"2":{"en":"for"},"3":{"en":"at"},"4":{"en":"with"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: “Engage with” means interact or communicate meaningfully with someone.</b><br>Tourists should engage respectfully with host communities.<br>“Engage to” and “engage for” do not express interaction.<br>“At” is not the required preposition in this construction.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): with.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};